1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Summary for Konrad I "der Grosse" Markgraf von Meissen =
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents:'''
2 CONT * Father: Thiemo II, Graf von Wettin (b. 1010/1015 or c. 1034 - d. after 1099/1101) or Thimo III "der Jungere" (the Brave), Graf von Brehna (c. 1055 - d. 1118/1124)
2 CONT *Mother: Ida von Northeim or Bertha von Groitzsch (a.k.a. Berta von Morungen) (b. ? - d. 1144)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings:'''
2 CONT *1. Dedo IV (d. 16 December 1124) Graf von Wettin, Graf von Groitzsch. m. Berta von Morungen (d. 16 June 1144), daughter of WIPRECHT [II] Graf von Groitzsch, Markgraf von Meissen and Judith of Bohemia.
2 CONT *3. Mathilde (d. 22 January 1155), m1. Gero, Graf von Seeburg, m2. Ludwig II von Wippra.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse:'''  
2 CONT *Luitgard von Elchingen (d. 19 June 1145 at Kloster Geberstedt, daughter of Adalbert, Graf von Elchingen-Ravenstein, and Bertha)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT *1. Heinrich (died young).
2 CONT *2. Otto "der Reiche" (c1125 - 18 February 1190), Markgraf von Meissen, zu Colditz und Lausick (present Leipzig, 1156-1190)
2 CONT *3. Oda (d. 2 June, unknown year), Abbess of Gerbstedt in 1137.
2 CONT *4. Berta, Abbess of Gerbstedt in 1190.
2 CONT *5. Dietrich (d. 9 February 1185), Markgraf der Niederlausitz und Graf von Eilenburg (1156-1185), m. in 1142 Dobronega Ludgarda of Poland. Had mistress Kunigunde from Bayern after October 1147.
2 CONT *6. Posibly Gertrud. m. Hermann von Stahleck (d. 2 October 1156), Graf von Stahleck and Pfalzgraf von Lothringen (1138-1155), brother of Konrad III, King of Germany.
2 CONT *7. Adelheid (d. after 6 December 1172), m1. in 1152, Svend III Erikssen "Grade", King of Denmark, repudiated 1153, m2. at the end of 1157 Albrecht, Graf von Ballenstedt.
2 CONT *8. Heinrich I (b. before 27 February 1142, d. 30 August 1181), Graf von Wettin (1156-1181) m. Sophie.
2 CONT *9. Dedo V "der Feiste" (d. 16 August 1190), Graf von Groitzsch (1144-1190)
2 CONT *10. Agnes (d. 21 January 1203) Abbess of Quedlinburg (1184-1203)
2 CONT *11. Sophie (d. 16 April after 1190) m. Gebhard I, Graf von Burghausen.
2 CONT *12. Friedrich I (27 February 1142 / 19 May 1145 - 4 January 1191), Graf von Brehna (1156-1191)
2 CONT
2 CONT = Basic information =
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birth:''' c. 1097 - Probably Wettin, Neletize, Mark Lusiza, Herzogtum Sachsen, Heiliges Römisches Reich. (FMG suggests 1097/1098, English Wikipedia suggests c1097, while Peerage suggests c1098.)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baptism:''' Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriages:''' before 1119 with Liutgard von Elchingen (FMG)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Death:''' 5 February 1157 - Kloster Petersberg, Petersburg bei Halle, Mark Merseburg, Herzogtum Sachsen, Heiliges Römisches Reich (FMG and Peerage, according to the German Wikipedia page for Petersberg, the Lauterberg name was 
2 CONC not attached to the monastery until the 14th century, though it appears in other Wikipedia pages and FMG)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Burial:''' FMG says Kloster Petersberg. At the time that he died, the Stiftskirche St. Petrus was under construction at the monastery (work began in 1142 and was completed in 1184). It would be reasonable to assume that burials
2 CONC  for Kloster Petersberg would have begun in the church yard sometime before his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Occupation:'''
2 CONT *Graf von Wettin
2 CONT *Graf von Brehna und Camburg (before 1116 to 1156)
2 CONT *Graf von Eilenburg (1123 - 1156)
2 CONT *Markgraf von Meissen in (1123 - 1156)
2 CONT *Resident of Kloster Petersberg (1156-1157)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alternate name:''' Konrad "der Grosse", Conrad "the Great" (the "von Meissen" was apparently taken from his most highest title, and may or may not have been used by his contemporaries to refer to him)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Medlands Project page on Meissen (covering his '''birth family'''):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEISSEN.htm#KonradIdied1157A
2 CONT
2 CONT '''THIMO''', son of DIETRICH Graf in Eilenburg, Graf im Hassegau und Siusli [Wettin] & his wife Mathilde von Meissen (-after [1099/1101]).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names "filios: Fridericum, Dedonem, Thiemonem, Geronem, Conradum, Riddagum, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus"[280].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni names "Thiemonem" as son of "Tidericus
2 CONC  comes" & his wife[281].  
2 CONT *'''Graf von Brehna'''.  
2 CONT *Vogt of Stift Gerbstedt.  
2 CONT *Co-founder of Naumburg cathedral. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1086]) '''IDA von Northeim''', daughter of OTTO [II] Graf von Northeim Duke of Bavaria & his wife Richenza of Swabia [Ezzonen].  
2 CONT *The Annales Stadenses refers to the four daughters of Otto, specifying that "una mater fuit Conradi de Witin marchionis" without naming her[282].  The Annales Magdeburgenses name "secunda [filia Ottonis ducis de Northeim] Ida" as
2 CONC  wife of "Thiemoni comiti de Witin"[283].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Idam filiam Othonis ducis de Northeim" as wife of "Thiemo comes"[284]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Thimo & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.   DEDO [IV] (-16 Dec 1124).  
2 CONT *The Annales Magdeburgenses name "Dedum comitem et Cuonradum marchionem" as the two sons of "Thiemoni comiti de Witin" and his wife Ida von Northeim[285].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Dedonem comitem et Conradum et filiam n
2 CONC omine Machthildem" as the children of "Thiemo comes" & his wife[286].  
2 CONT *Graf von Wettin.  
2 CONT *Graf von Groitzsch by right of his wife.  The Genealogica Wettinensis specifies that "Dedo filius Thiemonis" founded "ecclesiam in honore beati Petri apostolorum" but that its consecration was left because of the death of his bro
2 CONC ther Konrad[287].  
2 CONT *Founded Kloster Petersberg bei Halle in der Saale, of which he was Vogt.  
2 CONT *m (repudiated) BERTA von Morungen, daughter of WIPRECHT [II] Graf von Groitzsch [later Markgraf von Meissen] & his first wife Judith of Bohemia (-Monte Serreno 16 Jun 1144).  The Chronicon Montis Serreni names "Berta filia Wipert
2 CONC i marchionis de Groitz" as wife of "Dedo comes filius Thiemonis comitis"[288].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Bertham filiam Wiperti de Groitz" as wife of "Dedo filius Thiemonis", specifying that she was repudiated by her hus
2 CONC band and found refuge at Monte Serreno where she died[289].  The same source in a later passage records the death "1144 XVII Kal Iun" of "Berta comitissa filia Wiperti, uxor Dedonis comitis"[290].  Heiress of Burg Groitzsch.  The 
2 CONC Annales Pegavienses record the death in 1143 of "Berchta de Morunham, filia Wicperti marchionis"[291].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni records the death "1144 XVII Kal Iun" of "Berta comitissa, uxor Dedonis comitis"[292].  
2 CONT *Graf Dedo [IV] & his wife had one child: Mathilde (d. 1152, m. Rapoto II, Graf von Abensberg) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. '''KONRAD [I] "der Grosse"''' ([1097/98]-Kloster Petersberg 5 Feb 1157, bur Kloster Petersberg).  
2 CONT *The Annales Magdeburgenses name "Dedum comitem et Cuonradum marchionem" as the two sons of "Thiemoni comiti de Witin" and his wife Ida von Northeim[294].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Dedonem comitem et Conradum et filiam n
2 CONC omine Machthildem" as the children of "Thiemo comes" & his wife[295].  
2 CONT *Graf von Wettin.  
2 CONT *Graf von Brehna und Camburg before 1116.  
2 CONT *Graf von Eilenburg 1123.  
2 CONT *'''Markgraf von Meissen''' in 1123. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.  MATHILDE (-22 Jan 1155, bur Kloster Petersberg).  
2 CONT *The Gesta Archiepiscoporum Magdeburgensium names "Mechildis, soror Conradi comitis de Misen" as wife of "Gero comes de Seborch"[296].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Dedonem comitem et Conradum et filiam nomine Machthildem" a
2 CONC s the children of "Thiemo comes" & his wife, naming "Gero comes de Bavaria" as first husband of Mathilde and "Ludowicus comes de Bavaria, pater Ludowici abbatis Merseburgensis et Ludowicis comitis, patris Conradi prepositi" as her
2 CONC  second husband[297].  
2 CONT *Assuming that her first marriage is correct, she was the first cousin of her husband's maternal grandfather, which seems surprising.  
2 CONT *m firstly GERO Graf von Seeburg, son of WICHMANN Graf von Seeburg & his second wife Bertha von Camburg (12 Jul 1097-19 Sep 1133, bur Kloster Kaldenborn).  m secondly LUDWIG [II] von Wippra, son of --- (-1151).
2 CONT
