1 NAME Rudolf IV /von Diepholz/
2 GIVN Rudolf IV
2 SURN von Diepholz
2 _MARNM von Diepholz
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1278
2 PLAC Diepholz, Hannover, Tyskland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1350
1 OCCU Burgmann zu Vechta
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1310–1350: Rudolf IV, son of Konrad V, married Jutta of Oldenburg-Delmenhorst, daughter of Otto II, Count of Oldenburg in Delmenhorst.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rudolf IV, succeeded his father as sovereign of Diepholz in 1484, thanks to the premature death of his older brother, Konrad XI (died 1483), who had left progeny by an unknown partner. Konrad XI's son, Otto von Diepholt, married t
2 CONC he Frisian noblewoman, Anna Remets Ubbena, sister of Dr. Hayo "Hermannus Phrysius" Hompen, humanist scholar, Imperial Councillor and correspondent of Erasmus,[35] and half-sister of Wilhelm Ubbena, Chancellor of East-Frisia.[36]
2 CONT
2 CONT Konrad V's son, Rudolf IV (cited 1300-1350), continued to actively extend his possessions by his forceful and considered interventions during a very tumultuous period in the region.[17] In 1350, together with his sons and grandchi
2 CONC ldren, he founded the parish church of Diepholz (which had previously been in Drebber), which he dedicated to Saints Nicholas, Catherine and Elisabeth.[18]
2 CONT  Nieberding, C.H., Geschichte des ehemaligen Niederstifts Münster und der angränzenden Grafschaften Diepholz, Wildeshausen, etc., Vechta 1840 (reprinted 1967), p. 125.
