2 NOTE :D ok, I put your link in the info of the mentioned profile..
3 CONT ..but this JPG was to show at Curators the problems to be solved graphically, which when written to them seemed not to understand. But then in the end, I settled myself.
3 CONT  Following all the wrong snake has served to solve the problems caused by grafting overhead [1/6], & below in the tail [6/6], but above all behind the knot of marriage [1/6] had been confused Loraio II, king of Loritaringia (835-8
3 CONC 69) whit Lothair II of Arles, king of Italy (937-950) with shared children.
3 CONT since the 2 are also great-grandchildren via maternal line.. there was a really great mess of the pipe :) 
