4 CONC  Königtitels sowie den territorialen Zugewinn durch die Eroberung Österreichs die Grundlage für den weiteren Aufstieg seiner Familie. Er gilt außerdem als eine der populärsten Herrscherfiguren des deutschen Mittelalters.
4 CONT
4 CONT Rudolf of Habsburg (* May 1 1218 at Limburg Castle in Sasbach the emperor chair , † 15 July 1291 in Speyer ) was as Rudolf IV , Count of Habsburg , Kyburg and Lowenstein and Landgraf in Thurgau . As Rudolf I , he was from 1273, th
4 CONC e first Roman-German king of the sex of the Habsburgs , 1276-1286 also Duke of Carinthia and Carniola from 1278 to 1282 and Duke of Austria and Styria .
4 CONT Rudolf was the first - but only by Bernd Schneidmüller so - called " Earl King ". His achievements have been recognized by his contemporaries. He ended the interregnum , defeated the Bohemian King Ottokar II , and put the public p
4 CONC eace and the Hofrechtsprechung in parts of the empire again through. Within its means he strengthened the monarchy, despite the prominent position of the electors , and laid by winning the title of king and the territorial gains b
4 CONC y the conquest of Austria, the basis for the further advancement of his family. He is also considered one of the most popular figures of the German Middle Ages ruler.
