1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Heinrich III Graf zu Stolberg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Heinrich II von Stolberg, Graf von Stolberg and Adelheid von Henneberg 
2 CONT * During the Peasants' War , Hohnstein was still considered a safe fortress and was therefore visited by the abbot of Ilfeld Monastery to save himself and the monastery treasure. While the Counts of Hohnstein sealed the end of the
2 CONC ir rule at Lohra Castle (they died out in 1593), Hohnstein Castle came into the possession of the Counts of Stolberg through purchase in the 1st quarter of the 15th century , who took the complex militarily and structurally at gre
2 CONC at expense modernized (artillery tower) and expanded under [https://de.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burg_Hohnstein_(Harz) '''Count Heinrich zu Stolberg to a representative Renaissance castle.'''] During this time it became one of the larg
2 CONC est castles in the Harz Mountains.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897519716&photo_id=6000000165153393821&position=1 '''Heinrich III Graf zu Stolberg Geneology''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Jutta von Hadmersleben, '''circa 1270.4 Heinrich III, Graf & Herr von Stolberg married Jutta von Hadmersleben, daughter of Bodo von Hadmersleben and Irmgard von Beichlingen, after 29 July 1306 at of Stolberg, Sachsen
2 CONC , Prussia.1,2 Heinrich III, Graf & Herr von Stolberg died between 22 August 1329 and 29 August 1331. Heinrich V. zu Stolberg (–1329/1347) und Jutta von Hadmersleben (–1347);
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Friedrich 'the Elder' zu Stolberg,'''d. 12 Sep 1322
2 CONT * '''Bodo zu Stolberg,'''d. 3 Nov 1356
2 CONT * '''Friedrich 'the Younger' zu Stolberg,''' d. a 1347
2 CONT * '''Luitgard zu Hakeborn,'''d. 19 Dec 1353
2 CONT * '''Otto, Count of Stolberg,'''+ b. c 1310, d. bt 24 Nov 1337 - 10 Jan 1341
2 CONT * '''Heinrich V, Graf von Stolberg,''' b. c 1320, d. 13 Dec 1377
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/THURINGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc512066384 Project MedLands, THURINGIAN NOBILITY]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''HEINRICH [V] von Stolberg''' .  Graf von Stolberg.  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ
2 CONC , Irmengardis, Iuttæ et fratrum Theodorici, Friderici et Henrici”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[992].  “Heinricus...comes in Stalberg” donated property to the chapel of St. Johann at Schloß Stolberg, with the consent of “Henrici e
2 CONC t Henrici filiorum nostrorum seniorum et aliorum filiorum nostrorum”, by charter dated 7 Oct 1316, witnessed by “Henricus germanus noster canonicus ecclesiæ Herbipolensis, frater Elgerus ordinis minorum germanus noster...”[993].  
2 CONC '''married JUTTA,.'''  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ, Irmengardis, Iuttæ et fratrum 
2 CONC Theodorici, Friderici et Henrici”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[994].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Heinrich [V] & his wife JUTTA had [nine or more] children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''HEINRICH [VII] von Stolberg .'''  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ, Irm
2 CONC engardis, Iuttæ...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[995].  “Heinricus...comes in Stalberg” donated property to the chapel of St. Johann at Schloß Stolberg, with the consent of “Henrici et Henrici filiorum nostrorum seniorum et alior
2 CONC um filiorum nostrorum”, by charter dated 7 Oct 1316, witnessed by “Henricus germanus noster canonicus ecclesiæ Herbipolensis, frater Elgerus ordinis minorum germanus noster...”[996]. 
2 CONT * b)         '''HEINRICH [VIII] von Stolberg .'''  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ, Ir
2 CONC mengardis, Iuttæ...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[997].  “Heinricus...comes in Stalberg” donated property to the chapel of St. Johann at Schloß Stolberg, with the consent of “Henrici et Henrici filiorum nostrorum seniorum et alio
2 CONC rum filiorum nostrorum”, by charter dated 7 Oct 1316, witnessed by “Henricus germanus noster canonicus ecclesiæ Herbipolensis, frater Elgerus ordinis minorum germanus noster...”[998]. 
2 CONT * c)         '''AGNES von Stolberg.'''  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ, Irmengardis, 
2 CONC Iuttæ...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[999]. 
2 CONT * d)         '''SOPHIA von Stolberg .'''  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ, Irmengardis
2 CONC , Iuttæ...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[1000]. 
2 CONT * e)         '''ODA von Stolberg .'''  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ, Irmengardis, I
2 CONC uttæ...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[1001]. 
2 CONT * f)          '''ERMENGARD von Stolberg .'''  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ, Irmenga
2 CONC rdis, Iuttæ...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[1002]. 
2 CONT * g)         '''JUTTA von Stolberg'''  “Henricus comes in Stolberg” donated property “in Badra” to Kloster Walkenried, with the consent of “coniugis Iutta, filiorum Henrici et Henrici, filiarum Agnetis, Sophiæ, Odæ, Irmengardis, I
2 CONC uttæ...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1303[1003]. 
2 CONT * h)         '''Sons''' .  “Heinricus...comes in Stalberg” donated property to the chapel of St. Johann at Schloß Stolberg, with the consent of “Henrici et Henrici filiorum nostrorum seniorum et aliorum filiorum nostrorum”, by cha
2 CONC rter dated 7 Oct 1316, witnessed by “Henricus germanus noster canonicus ecclesiæ Herbipolensis, frater Elgerus ordinis minorum germanus noster...”[1004]. 
2 CONT
