2 CONC of Otto of Northeim.[1][2] Thimo is buried at Niemegk Monastery, which he had founded.
2 CONT
2 CONT The exact year of Thimo's death is unclear; since his son Conrad was born in approximately 1098, Thiemo cannot have died long before this year. Alternatively, some researchers assume that Thimo was in fact Conrad's grandfather, an
