1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Andrey Glebovich - according to historian Boguslavsky, prince of Ryazan, the eldest son of Gleb Rostislavich, the prince of Ryazan, and Euphrosyne (Evfrosinya) Rostislavna, daughter of Pereyaslav prince Rostislav Y
2 CONC urievich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrey was mentioned in the annals only once in 1184(without a patronymic and occupation) as a participant in the successful battle of Igor Svyatoslavich, prince of Novgorod-Seversky, with the Polovtsians on the Khiriya River.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some researchers believe that Andrey Glebovich died before 1186.
