1 TITL prince
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Vladimir Glebovich''' (d. after 1196) - prince of Pronsk.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Together with his older brothers Roman and Igor, he owned the Ryazan principality, although, the Ryazan throne went to Roman as an older brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1180, together with his brother Vsevolod, with the support of Vsevolod the Big Nest, he participated in civil strife against the brothers Roman and Igor.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1183 he went with Vsevolod to the Volga-Kama Bulgars.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1186, sitting with the brothers Roman and Igor on the Ryazan reign, he went with them to his other brothers - Vsevolod and Svyatoslav - the princes of Pronsk, and laid siege to Pronsk. Not listening to the grand-ducal ambassado
2 CONC rs who urged the brothers to reconcile, the latter entered into battle with the advanced detachments of the Grand Duke, who supported the Pronsky princes, but, having heard about the approach of the main forces of Vsevolod the Big
2 CONC  Nest to Pronsk, Vladimir Glebovich, together with his brothers, fled from the walls of the city. But as soon as the help left, he returned and captured the city, luring his brother Svyatoslav to his side. He sent to the Grand Duk
2 CONC e to ask for peace but was refused.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1187, together with his brothers, he sent the Bishop of Chernigov Porfiry to Vsevolod to intercede for himself and achieved peace.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1195, he was present in Vladimir at the wedding of Konstantin, son of Vsevolod the Big Nest.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1196, he went with Vsevolod the Big Nest to the Chernigov Principality.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Gleb Rostislavich (d. 1178) - Prince of Ryazan (1145-1177 intermittently).
2 CONT Mother: Euphrosyne (Evfrosinya) Rostislavna (d. 1179) - daughter of Rostislav Yuryevich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brothers and sisters:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Andrey? (d. before 1186) - mentioned only once prior to Roman Glebovich in the chronicle of 1184, although Roman was a prince of Ryazan from 1178 to 1207.
2 CONT * Roman (d. 1216) - Grand Duke of Ryazan (1180-1207).
2 CONT * Igor (d. 1195) - principal prince of Ryazan.
2 CONT * Theodosia - married to Mstislav the Brave.
2 CONT * Vsevolod (d. 1207) - prince of Pronsk (until 1186, 1188-1207) and Kolomna (1186-1188).
2 CONT * Svyatoslav (d. after 1207) - principal prince of Pronsk.
2 CONT * Yaroslav (d. after 1199) - prince of Ryazan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Gleb (d. 1219) - prince of Ryazan (1212-1217), organizer of the fratricidal Congress in Isady, where he killed 6 princes (brother and cousins)
2 CONT # Oleg (d. before 1217) - prince of Pronsk (1207-before 1217).
2 CONT # Izyaslav (d. 1217) - prince of Pronsk (1207) - was killed in Isady by his brother.
2 CONT # Constantine (d. after 1217) -  titled prince of Pronsk, helped Gleb to organize the murder. (His middle name is not indicated in the sources, there is some possibility that he is not the son of Vladimir, but a nephew)
