1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander Nevsky
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Novgorod First Chronicle, Alexander married first a daughter of Bryacheslav Vasilkovich, Prince of Polatsk and Vitebsk, in 1239. Her name is not given in the chronicle. Genealogies name her as Paraskeviya or Alexa
2 CONC ndra. Possibly birth and marital names respectively. They had at least five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Vasily Aleksandrovich, Prince of Novgorod (c. 1239 - 1271). He was betrothed to Princess Kristina of Norway in 1251. The marriage contact was broken. Kristina went on to marry Felipe of Castile, a son of Ferdinand III of Castile a
2 CONC nd Elisabeth of Hohenstaufen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudoxia Aleksandrovna. Married Konstantin Rostislavich, Prince of Smolensk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dmitry of Pereslavl (c. 1250 - 1294).
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrey of Gorodets (c. 1255 - 27 July 1304
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel of Moscow (1261 - 4 March/5 March 1303).
