1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vladimir in 1188 stole wife from Russian Pope (Orthodox priest) took her for himself as a second wife, and with her had 2 sons: Vasilko and Vladimir (Ivan). There was assassination attempt on Vasilko and his new wi
2 CONC fe Teodora (Fedora), organised by boyars in rebellion.  Later these two sons were taken together with their father as a prisoners by Hungarians. There was mentioning of their escape in some sources, but their later fate is unknown
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Papal (Roman Pope) letter of 1218, confirms the donation to the monastery in Hungary. In this letter the depositors to the monastery are mentioned as some «Basilica et Iohanne Blandemero», who may be the sons of the Galician princ
2 CONC e Vladimir:
2 CONT * Basilo = Vasili, 
2 CONT * Iohanne = Ivan.
