1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lambert von Gleichen († 1272 ) was a prophet at the Neumünster Abbey from 1258 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lambert stemmed from a Thuringian nobility family and was proclaimed in 1248 by Bishop Hermann I of Lobdeburg in Erfurt. Since April 16, 1258 , he has been a witness to the Neumünster Abbey. In 1264 , he received a papal canon at 
2 CONC the penitent, since he had arrested two forgers of pope tales. However, he could not compete with the Canon, since it contradicted the statutes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source; http://wuerzburgwiki.de/wiki/Lambert_von_Gleichen
