1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sternberg_(Adelsgeschlecht) wikipedia] (google translation) 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Peter von Konopischt and Sternberg''' (Petr Konopišťský ze Šternberka) (​​ - 11/1/1420) son of '''Markvart von Sternberg''' inherited after his father and his brothers, half the assets of '''Sternberger''' from his Uncle '''Alb
2 CONC ert Konopischt''' and the second half of the Sternberg-lands. 1415, he married '''Perchta of''' [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krava%C5%99 '''Kravař''''] (Perchta z Kravaře). He was an ardent advocate of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wi
2 CONC ki/Hussite Hussite]. 1414 he accompanied [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_von_Bucca Johann von Bucca] to the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Constance Council of Constance]. Later he took the side of the [http://en.wi
2 CONC kipedia.org/wiki/Hussite_Wars Hussite Wars] royalists attended, among others in [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nov%C3%BD_Kn%C3%ADn Nový Knín] (Knin) in 1419, 1420, he fought alongside the Emperor in the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wik
2 CONC i/Battle_of_Sudom%C4%9B%C5%99 Battle of Sudoměř] and [http://de.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Po%C5%99%C3%AD%C4%8D%C3%AD_nad_S%C3%A1zavou&action=edit&redlink=1 Parschnitz]. He fell at the Battle of Pankrac on the side of the arm
2 CONC ies of the Bohemian [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigismund,_Holy_Roman_Emperor Holy Roman Emperor Sigismund]. He left two sons ('''Peter''' and '''Zdeniek''' whose legitimate origin is not confirmed) and daughter '''Elizabeth''',
2 CONC  who died after 1421. Son '''Peter''' followed her 1439 
