4 CONT Ludwig († 1305).
4 CONT Furthermore Meinhard had numerous extramarital offspring:
4 CONT Frederick, provost of Brixen († March 13, 1333), Anna Reichenberg married
4 CONT Henry, Earl of ash hole († 1349)
4 CONT Albrecht of Camian and Forestry, Viscount of Tyrol († 1335/36), with Floridiana (Siguna) of Schlandersberg married
4 CONT and another ten illegitimate children with hitherto unknown women
4 CONT Literature [ Edit ]
4 CONT
4 CONT Dream of a prince - the emergence of Tyrol. exhibition catalog of the exhibition at Castle Tyrol Tyrol and Stams, Dorf Tirol Innsbruck 1995.
4 CONT Wilhelm Baum: ., the Counts of Gorizia in European politics of the Middle Ages Kitab-Verlag, Klagenfurt, 2000. ISBN 3-902005-04-1
4 CONT Wilhelm Baum:  Meinhard II . In: New German Biography (NDB). Volume 16 Duncker & Humblot, Berlin 1990, ISBN 3-428-00197-4 , pp. 668 f ( digitized ).
4 CONT Alfons Huber:  Meinhard II . In: General German Biography (ADB). Volume 21, Duncker & Humblot, Leipzig, 1885, pp. 229-231.
4 CONT Hermann Wiesflecker: Meinhard the second. Tyrol, Carinthia and the neighboring countries of the 13th Century (Sciliar fonts 124). Wagner, Innsbruck 1995. ISBN 3-7030-0287-5
