1 NOTE Elisabeth de Gorizia de Tirol de Carantania (c. 1262 - 28 October 1312) was queen consort of the Holy Roman Empire and Duchess of Austria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT She was the eldest daughter of Meinhard II, Duke of Carinthia, count of Gorizia and Tyrol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother was Elisabeth of Bavaria. She was a daughter of Otto II Wittelsbach, Duke of Bavaria and his wife Agnes, herself daughter of Henry V, Count Palatine of the Rhine and Agnes of Hohenstaufen. Her mother was also the widow 
2 CONC of Conrad IV of Germany. Therefore, the young Elisabeth was a half-sister of Conradin, King of Jerusalem and Duke of Swabia.
2 CONT
2 CONT The younger Elisabeth was from 1274 the wife of the future Albert I of Germany, one of the founders of the House of Habsburg, thus becoming daughter-in-law of the King of the Romans. Her husband, then a Count of Habsburg was inves
2 CONC ted as Duke of Austria and Styria in December 1282 by his father the King Rudolf. They solidified their rule in what was to become the Habsburg patrimony, also by help of Elisabeth's father who in his turn in 1286 was created Duke
2 CONC  of Carinthia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1298, her husband was finally elected king upon the end of the reign of Adolf of Nassau. Her husband was murdered on 1 May 1308 by his nephew John "the Parricide" in Windisch, located in modern-day Switzerland.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT She was married in Vienna on 20 December 1274 to the future Albert I of Germany. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rudolph III (ca. 1282-4 July 1307, Horazdiowitz), Married but line extinct and predeceased his father. 
2 CONT Frederick I (1289-13 January 1330, Gutenstein). Married but line extinct. 
2 CONT Leopold I (4 August 1290-28 February 1326, Strassburg). Married but line extinct. 
2 CONT Albert II (12 December 1298, Vienna-20 July 1358, Vienna). 
2 CONT Heinrich (1299-3 February 1327, Bruck an der Mur). Married but line extinct. 
2 CONT Meinhard, 1300 died young. 
2 CONT Otto (23 July 1301, Vienna-26 February 1339, Vienna). Married but line extinct. 
2 CONT Anna 1280?, Vienna-19 March 1327, Breslau), married: 
2 CONT in Graz ca. 1295 to Margrave Hermann of Brandenburg; 
2 CONT in Breslau 1310 to Duke Heinrich VI of Breslau. 
2 CONT Agnes (18 May 1281-10 June 1364, Königsfelden), married in Vienna 13 February 1296 King Andrew III of Hungary. 
2 CONT Elisabeth (d. 19 May 1353), married 1304 Frederick IV, Duke of Lorraine. 
2 CONT Katharina (1295-18 January 1323, Naples), married 1316 Charles, Duke of Calabria. 
2 CONT Jutta (d. 1329), married in Baden 26 March 1319 Count Ludwig VI of Öttingen. 
