1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WURTTEMBERG.htm#AlbrechtHohenbergdied1298
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         '''ALBRECHT''' [II] "der Minnesänger" von Hohenberg (-killed in battle Oberndorf 17 Apr 1298, bur Klosterkirche Kirchberg bei Haigerloch).  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 1262 under which "Albertus…Come
2 CONC s de Hohenberc" confirmed a donation made in the presence of "pie memorie Comitis Burchardi…patris mei" to Kloster Rotenmünster[566].  Graf von Hohenberg.  Graf von Rotenburg 1264: "Albertus…comes de Rotinburg" resolved a dispute 
2 CONC involving Kloster Kreuzlingen by charter dated 1 Feb 1264[567].  "Alberthus, Burkardus, Ulricus, fratres…Comtes de Hohenberg" confirmed a sale of property to Kloster Kirchberg by charter dated 25 Oct 1269[568].  Graf von Haigerloc
2 CONC h 1272/1287.  “Albertus et Burcardus fratres comites de Hohenberg...et pro fratre nostro Ulrico” renounced rights “super curti...apud Nunburg in Brisgaudia” in favour of the bishop of Strasbourg by charter dated 26 Feb 1274[569]. 
2 CONC  The Annales Basilienses record that "dominus Hagineche" wounded "comitem de Hohinberch, cognatum regis" in 1277 in the king's presence[570].  In Hohenberg, Haigerloch und Rottenburg 1281.  Landrichter in Swabia 1278/1291.  Vogt v
2 CONC on Hirsau 1281.  “Elisabeth comitissa de Eberstein et de Tuwingen” bequeathed property “apud Horwe” to Reichenbach, with the consent of “mariti nostri Ottonis nobilis de Eberstein patruorum nostrorum Ottonis et Ludovici comit. Pal
2 CONC atini de Tuwingen”, by charter dated 26 Feb 1283, witnessed by “avunculi nostri Albertus et Burchardus com. de Hochinberg...”[571].  “Eberhardus quondam Rudolfi comitis palatini de Tuwingen filius dictus Scharer“ sold property to 
2 CONC Kloster Bebenhausen, with the consent of “fratris nostri Rudolfi comitis”, by charter dated 23 Apr 1289, witnessed by “avunculi nostri Alberti de Hohenberch et...Cunradi de Vahingen comitum”[572].  The Annales Sancti Udalrici et A
2 CONC fræ Augustenses record that "Otto dux Bavarie" killed "comitem de Heigerloch" in 1297[573].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ---.  The name of Albrecht's first wife is not known.  The following charter suggests that she may have been the aunt of Diepold [II] Graf von Aichelberg, although the precise family relationship indicated by the t
2 CONC erm “avunculus” has not in this case been ascertained: "Graf Diepold von Aichelberg" donated property in Mannsberg to Kloster Baindt, for the souls of his parents, by charter dated 1282, sealed (in the absence of his own seal) by 
2 CONC the seal of “Alberti comitis de Hohemberc avunculi mei”[574].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (Hohenfriedingen 19 Jul 1282) MARGARETA von Fürstenberg, daughter of HEINRICH [I] Graf von Fürstenberg & his wife Agnes von Truhendingen (-1296, bur Klosterkirche Kirchberg bei Haigerloch).  The Annales Sindelfing
2 CONC enses record the marriage of "comes Albertus in Onfridingen XIV Kal Aug 1282" but do not name his wife[575].  "Albertus Comes de Hohenberg et Margaretha coniux eiusdem" donated property to Kloster Kirchberg by charter dated 12 Jul
2 CONC  1291[576].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m thirdly URSULA von Oettingen, daughter of [LUDWIG [III] Graf von Oettingen & his first wife --- von Burgau] (-1308, bur Ehingen).  
2 CONT
2 CONT     Graf Albrecht [II] & his first wife had four children:
2 CONT   Graf Albrecht [II] & his second wife had [four] children:
2 CONT   Graf Albrecht [II] & his second wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT
