1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elisabeth of Meissen=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Elisabeth of Meissen, Burgravine of Nuremberg (22 November 1329 – 21 April 1375) was the daughter of Frederick II, Margrave of Meissen and Mathilde of Bavaria and a member of the House of Wettin.
2 CONT * Elisabeth Prinzessin von Bayern-Landshut gained the title of Prinzessin von Bayern-Landshut.
2 CONT * Birth:	November 22, 1329 in Wartburg,Sachsen-Weimar-Eisenach,Thüringen,Germany, Nürnberg
2 CONT * Death:	April 21, 1375 (45) in Kloster Heilbronn, Middlefranken, Bavaria, Germany, Nürnberg
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: at the age of twenty six, '''Friedrich I Kurfürst von Brandenburg,''' son of Friedrich V Markgraf von Brandenburg and Elisabeth Prinzessin von Bayern-Landshut, in 1401. 
2 CONT * Together Frederick and Elisabeth had eight children, six girls and two boys, who survived to adulthood:
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Elisabet,''' (1358–26 July 1411, Heidelberg), married in Amberg 1374 to Rupert of Germany.
2 CONT * '''Beatrix''' (c. 1362, Nuremberg–10 June 1414, Perchtoldsdorf), married in Vienna 1375 Duke Albert III of Austria
2 CONT * '''Anna''' (c. 1364–after 10 May 1392), a nun in Seusslitz.
2 CONT * '''Agnes''' (1366 – 22 May 1432), Convent in Hof (1376–1386) married in Konstance 1386 Baron Friedrich of Daber, Returned to Convent in Hof (1406) Abbess in Hof (1411–1432).
2 CONT * '''John''' (c. 1369–11 June 1420, Plassenburg).
2 CONT *''' Frederick I, Elector of Brandenburg'''  born, 21 September 1371 in Free Imperial City of Nuremberg & died 20 September 1440 (aged 68) in Cadolzburg Castle, Principality of Ansbach Frederick (Middle High German: Friderich, Sta
2 CONC ndard German: Friedrich; 21 September 1371 – 20 September 1440) was the last Burgrave of Nuremberg from 1397 to 1427 (as Frederick VI), Margrave of Brandenburg-Ansbach from 1398, Margrave of Brandenburg-Kulmbach from 1420, and Ele
2 CONC ctor of Brandenburg (as Frederick I) from 1415 until his death. He became the first member of the House of Hohenzollern to rule the Margraviate of Brandenburg.
2 CONT * '''Margarete''' (died 1406, Gudensberg), married in Kulmbach 1383 Landgrave Hermann of Hesse.
2 CONT * '''Katharina''' (died 1409), Abbess in Hof.
2 CONT * '''Veronica of Hohenzollern,''' married Barnim VI, Duke of Pomerania.
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth''' died at the age of 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elisabeth_of_Meissen Elisabeth of Meissen, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth of Meissen, Burgravine of Nuremberg (22 November 1329 – 21 April 1375) was the daughter of Frederick II, Margrave of Meissen and Mathilde of Bavaria and a member of the House of Wettin.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Wartburg. On 7 September 1356, at the age of twenty six, she married Frederick V, Burgrave of Nuremberg in Jena. In 1357 her husband succeeded to the title, and from that time until her death in 1375, she was style
2 CONC d as Burgravine of Nuremberg. Together Frederick and Elisabeth had eight children, six girls and two boys, who survived to adulthood:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth''' (1358–26 July 1411, Heidelberg), married in Amberg 1374 to Rupert of Germany.
2 CONT * '''Beatrix''' (c. 1362, Nuremberg–10 June 1414, Perchtoldsdorf), married in Vienna 1375 Duke Albert III of Austria
2 CONT * '''Anna''' (c. 1364–after 10 May 1392), a nun in Seusslitz.
2 CONT * '''Agnes''' (1366 – 22 May 1432), Convent in Hof (1376–1386) married in Konstance 1386 Baron Friedrich of Daber, Returned to Convent in Hof (1406) Abbess in Hof (1411–1432).
2 CONT * '''John''' (c. 1369–11 June 1420, Plassenburg).
2 CONT * '''Frederick''' (1371–1440).
2 CONT * '''Margarete''' (died 1406, Gudensberg), married in Kulmbach 1383 Landgrave Hermann of Hesse.
2 CONT * '''Katharina''' (died 1409), Abbess in Hof.
2 CONT * '''Veronica of Hohenzollern,''' married Barnim VI, Duke of Pomerania.
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth''' died at the age of 45.
2 CONT
