1 TITL Queen
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elisabeth, Burggravine of Nuremberg, was the daughter of Frederick V, Burgrave of Nuremberg and Elisabeth of Meissen. She was a member of the House of Hohenzollern.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in 1358, and on 27 June 1374 married Rupert, then heir to the Elector Palatine, Rupert II. Elisabeth became Electress Palatine when Rupert succeeded to his father's estate 6 January 1398, and Queen of the Romans when 
2 CONC Rupert was elected King of the Romans on 21 August 1400. Rupert died on 18 May 1410; Elisabeth survived him by a little over a year, dying on 26 July 1411.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth and Rupert had nine children, six sons and three daughters, who survived to adulthood:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rupert Pipan (20 February 1375, Amberg – 25 January 1397, Amberg). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (1376 – 27 August 1434, Nancy), married in 1394 to Charles II, Duke of Lorraine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick (ca. 1377, Amberg – 7 March 1401, Amberg). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (23 January 1378 – 30 December 1436, Heidelberg). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes (1379 – 1401, Heidelberg), married in Heidelberg shortly before March 1400 to Duke Adolf of Kleve. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth (27 October 1381 – 31 December 1408, Innsbruck), married in Innsbruck 24 December 1407 to Duke Frederick IV of Austria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John (1383, Neunburg vorm Wald – 13–14 March 1443). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen (23 June 1385 – 14 February 1459, Simmern). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto (24 August 1390, Mosbach – 5 July 1461). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth of Nuremberg
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth, Burggravine of Nuremberg, was the daughter of Frederick V, Burgrave of Nuremberg and Elisabeth of Meissen. She was a member of the House of Hohenzollern.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in 1358, and on 27 June 1374 married Rupert, then heir to the Elector Palatine, Rupert II. Elisabeth became Electress Palatine when Rupert succeeded to his father's estate 6 January 1398, and Queen of the Romans when 
2 CONC Rupert was elected King of the Romans on 21 August 1400. Rupert died on 18 May 1410; Elisabeth survived him by a little over a year, dying on 26 July 1411.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth and Rupert had nine children, six sons and three daughters, who survived to adulthood:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rupert Pipan (20 February 1375, Amberg – 25 January 1397, Amberg).
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (1376 – 27 August 1434, Nancy), married in 1394 to Charles II, Duke of Lorraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick (ca. 1377, Amberg – 7 March 1401, Amberg).
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (23 January 1378 – 30 December 1436, Heidelberg).
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes (1379 – 1401, Heidelberg), married in Heidelberg shortly before March 1400 to Duke Adolf of Kleve.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth (27 October 1381 – 31 December 1408, Innsbruck), married in Innsbruck 24 December 1407 to Duke Frederick IV of Austria.
2 CONT
2 CONT John (1383, Neunburg vorm Wald – 13–14 March 1443).
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen (23 June 1385 – 14 February 1459, Simmern).
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto (24 August 1390, Mosbach – 5 July 1461).
