2 CONT Albert II, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg; c. 1268 – 22 September 1318), called the Fat (pinguis), was duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT The second son of Albert the Tall, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg, Albert was a boy when his father died in 1279. He was first under guardianship of his uncle, Conrad, Bishop of Verden, and then of his elder brother, Henry I, Duke of 
2 CONC Brunswick-Lüneburg. In 1286 the three brothers divided their father's territory; Albert received the areas around Göttingen, Minden, Northeim, Calenberg, and Hanover. He made Göttingen his residence. In 1292, the third brother, Wi
2 CONC lliam, died childless, and Albert and Henry quarrelled about William's share, the areas around Brunswick and Wolfenbüttel; Albert finally prevailed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert married Rixa, daughter of Henry I, Prince of Werle, in 1284. They had the following children who reached adulthood:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide, married John, Landgrave of Lower Hesse 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richenza, Abbess of Gandersheim 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mechtild 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jutta 
2 CONT
2 CONT Luder, joined the Teutonic Order 
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert II, Bishop of Halberstadt (died 1358) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry, Bishop of Hildesheim (died 1362) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto (died 1344) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus (died 1369) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernest (died 1367) 
2 CONT
