1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: Central France: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20FRANCE.htm#ThibautVdied1191B Blois, Tours]
2 CONT * 2. '''MARGUERITE''' ([1170]–12 Jul 1230). "…''Filiis quoque et filiabus meis Theobaldo et Ludovico atque Henrico, Margarita et Ysabella''" consented to the donation by "''Theobaldus Blesensis comes, Francie senesscalus''" to Hôt
2 CONC el-Dieu, Châteaudun by charter dated 1183[344]. "''Hugo vicecomes Meldensis''" donated property to Cavea monastery, with the consent of "''domina Margarete uxore mea''", by charter dated to [1185][345]. Her first marriage is confi
2 CONC rmed by the charter dated [Jun/Aug] 1208 under which "''Margareta uxor Galterii de Averna comitissa palatina Burgundie''" confirmed an agreement between "''Willelmum militem de Monasteriis''" and Saint-Martin-des-Champs which also
2 CONC  names "''Hugo de Oysi filius Symonis vicecomitis, olim maritus meus''"[346]. "''Hugo de Oisiaco vicecomes Meldensis, castellanus Cameracensis''" donated property to "''ecclesiam B. Mariæ de Pratis''", for the soul of "''uxoris me
2 CONC æ Margaretæ''", by charter dated 1189[347]. "''Filiabus mei Margarita, Ysabella''" consented to the donation by "''Theobaldus comes Blesensis, Francie senesscalus''" to Hôtel-Dieu, Châteaudun by charter dated 1190[348]. "…''Philip
2 CONC po fratre et sororibus Marguerita, Isabella et Adelicia''" consented to the donation by "''Louis C. de Blois et de Clermont''" to the abbey of l'Etoile by charter dated 1190[349]. William of Tyre (Continuator) records "''la fille 
2 CONC dou conte Thibaut de Blois''" being the wife of "''Otes dus de Borgoigne''"[350]. "…''Sororibus meis Margarita, Ysabella, Adelicis''" consented to the donation by "''Ludovicus comes Blesensis et Clarimontis''" to Hôtel-Dieu, Châte
2 CONC audun by charter dated 27 Jan 1196[351]. "…''Sororibusque meis Margarita et Ysabella et Adelicia''" consented to the confirmation by "''Ludovicus Blesensis et Clarimontis comes''" of the donation by "''Gaufridus vicecomes Castridu
2 CONC ni''" to Hôtel-Dieu, Châteaudun by charter dated Mar 1200[352]. The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis records that "''dominus Galterus filius [Jacobi] primogeniti''" married "''Margareta comitatus Blesensis hæred
2 CONC e''"[353]. "…''Sororibus meis Margarita, Ysabella''" consented to the donation by "''Ludovicus Blesensis et Clarimontis comes…Iherosolimam proficiscens''" to Hôtel-Dieu, Châteadun by charter dated May 1202[354]. "''Margareta uxor 
2 CONC Galterii de Averna comitissa palatina Burgundie''" confirmed an agreement between "''Willelmum militem de Monasteriis''" and Saint-Martin-des-Champs by charter dated [Jun/Aug] 1208 which also names "''Hugo de Oysi filius Symonis v
2 CONC icecomitis, olim maritus meus''"[355]. She succeeded her nephew in 1218 as Ctss de Blois et de Châteaudun. The necrology of the abbey of Vauduisant records the death "''IV Id Jul''" of "''comitisse Blesensis Marguerite''"[356]. Th
2 CONC e necrology of La Cour-Dieu records the death “''IV Id Jul''” of “''comitissa Blesensis''”[357]. 
2 CONT * '''m''' firstly ([1183]) as his second wife, [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfracado.htm#HuguesOisyCambraidied1189 '''HUGUES''' [III] '''d'Oisy'''] châtelain de Cambrai, son of SIMON d'Oisy, châtelain de Cambrai & his wife Ad
2 CONC a de la Ferté-Ancoul (-29 Aug 1189). 
2 CONT * '''m''' secondly ([1190]) [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDY%20Kingdom.htm#OthonIComtedied1200 '''OTTO von Staufen'''] Comte Palatin de Bourgogne, son of Emperor FRIEDRICH I "Barbarossa" & his second wife Beatrix Ctss Pa
2 CONC latine de Bourgogne ([Jun/Jul] 1170-Besançon 13 Jan 1200, bur Besançon Saint-Etienne). 
2 CONT * '''m''' thirdly (after 1200) [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HAINAUT.htm#WautierIIAvesnesdied12431246 '''GAUTHIER''' [II] '''d'Avesnes'''] Seigneur d'Avesnes, son of JACQUES Seigneur d'Avesnes & his wife Adeline de Guise (-[12
2 CONC 43/46]). Comte de Blois et de Guise. 
2 CONT
