2 CONT Hugh III of Chalon, Count of Burgundy (also known as Hugues de Bourgogne) (1220-1266) was count of Burgundy by his marriage to countess Adelaide I of Burgundy when he was aged 16, on 1 November 1236. He was the son of John, Count 
2 CONC of Chalon and his first wife Mahaud (or Mahaut) of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of his children was Reginald of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh III's wife remarried to Philip I, Count of Savoy a year after his death and she was succeeded as count by Otto, one of her children by Hugh.
