2 CONT
2 CONT Otto IV, Count of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto IV, Count of Burgundy (1248-1302) was the son of Hugh de Chalon and Adelaide, Countess Palatine of Burgundy. By his mother, he was a grandson of Countess Beatrice II of Burgundy. By his father, he was descended from another b
2 CONC ranch of the Counts of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his father's death in 1266/1267, he became Count of Chalons.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Philippa of Bar in 1271. The marriage was childless.
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother, Adelaide, died on March 8, 1279, and Otto inherited the County. However, he was unable to secure real power in the County until 1295.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married his second wife, Mahaut of Artois, in 1285. They had three children: Jeanne, Blanche, and Robert. Of these, his daughters would marry eventual Kings of France, and both his son and elder daughter were to succeed him in 
2 CONC the County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his death in 1302, his titles were inherited by his son.
