1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#DiepoldILeuchtenbergdied1209B
2 CONT
2 CONT GERHARD [IV] (-[21 Aug/2 Sep] 1279).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Landgraf von Leuchtenberg zu Falkenberg.  m  ELISABETH von Ortenburg, daughter of HEINRICH [I] Graf von Ortenburg 
2 CONC & his first wife Božislawa of Bohemia (-1272, bur Waldsassen).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  Landgraf Gerhard [IV] & his wife had [six or more] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          GERHARD [V] (-[12 Aug/10 Nov] 1293).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Landgraf von Leuchtenberg zu Falkenberg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -         see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         HEINRICH [I] (-after 8 Nov 1295).  Landgraf.  Canon at Regensburg 1279/80.  "Heinricus langravius de Leukenberge filius Gebhardi quondam langravii felicis recordationis" sold his part of "Liukenberge" to "domino nostro
2 CONC  Lodwico…comiti palatino Reni, duci Bawarie et…domine Mehthildi uxori eius…Romanorum regis filie", with the consent of "nostri fratris Friderici iunioris langravii", by charter dated 18 Nov 1282[838].  Teutonic Knight 1291/95. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)        FRIEDRICH [III] .  "Heinricus langravius de Leukenberge filius Gebhardi quondam langravii felicis recordationis" sold his part of "Liukenberge" to "domino nostro Lodwico…comiti palatino Reni, duci Bawarie et…domine Meh
2 CONC thildi uxori eius…Romanorum regis filie", with the consent of "nostri fratris Friderici iunioris langravii", by charter dated 18 Nov 1282[839].  Cistercian monk at Aldersbach 1307. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv)       KONRAD (-25 Jun <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Canon at Regensburg 1279/1300. 
2 CONT
2 CONT v)        daughters .  The primary source which confirms their parentage has not yet been identified.  1279.
