1 NAME Elisabeth /von Ortenburg/
2 GIVN Elisabeth
2 SURN von Ortenburg
2 _MARNM von Ortenburg
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1232
2 PLAC Ortenburg, Germany
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1272
2 PLAC Leuchtenberg, Germany
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#ElisabethOrtenburgdied1272
2 CONT
2 CONT HEINRICH [I] von Ortenburg (-15 Feb 1241).  "Rapoto Comes de Ortenberch" donated property to St Nikolas, for the soul of "patris sui Rapotonis comitis" in the presence of "Heinrico fratre suo et Comitissa matre eorum", by charter 
2 CONC dated to [1190][1154].  "Elisabeth cometissa in Ortenberc" donated property to Bamburg, for the soul of "mariti sui Rapotonis", by charter dated 1194, witnessed by "Comes Rapoto et frater eius Heinricus in Ortinberch…"[1155].  Gra
2 CONC f von Ortenburg.  "Comes Heinricus et filius eius Heinricus de Orttenberch" witnessed a donation to St Nikolas by charter dated 1237[1156].  The necrology of Baumburg records the death "XV Kal Mar" of "Hainricus com de Ortenburg"[
2 CONC 1157].  The necrology of Aldersbach records the death "XV Kal Mar" of "Heinrici com de Ortenberg"[1158].  The necrology of Asbach records the death "XV Kal Mar" of "Henericus com de Orttenburg"[1159].  m firstly BOŽISLAWA of Bohem
2 CONC ia, daughter of PŘEMYSL OTAKAR I King of Bohemia & his first wife Adelheid von Meissen [Wettin] (-6 Feb [1238 or before]).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Vredislaum et filias tres" as children of "Odacarus qui postea fuit dux
2 CONC  Bohemie" and his wife Adelheid, specifying that one daughter (mentioned second in the text) married "Heinrico comiti de Orthenberc"[1160].  A 13th century genealogy refers to the two daughters of "rex Boemie Otaker" and his wife 
2 CONC Adelheid, specifying that "alteram" married "Henricus de Hortenberch"[1161].  m secondly RICHIZA von Hohenburg, daughter of DIEPOLD [VII] Markgraf von Vohburg und Hohenburg & his wife Mechtild von Wasserburg (-1266).  Graf Heinric
2 CONC h [I] & his first wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ELISABETH von Ortenburg (-1272, bur Waldsassen).  m GEBHARD [IV] Landgraf von Leuchtenberg, son of GEBHARD [II] Landgraf von Leuchtenberg & his wife Elisabeth von Nürnberg (-[21 Aug/2 Sep] 1279).  
