1 NOTE {geni:about_me} m ---.  The primary source which confirms the identity of Otto’s wife has not been identified.  It is possible that she was named Kunigunde, as the necrology of Undensdorf records the death "IV Id Jul" of "Chunegun
2 CONC t com"[835].  This necrology records almost exclusively members of the Wittelsbach family and this entry cannot be linked to any other known person in the family.  Pfalzgraf Otto [III] & his wife had two children:  1.         OTTO
2 CONC  [IV] (-4/5 Aug 1156, bur Ensdorf).  “Perchtoldo de Esgilbach” exchanged property with Freising church, in the presence of “Ottonis advocatis et filii sui Ottonis”, by undated charter dated to the early 12th century[836].  Graf vo
2 CONC n Scheyern.  Pfalzgraf von Wittelsbach.  -        see below.  2.         daughter .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m OTTO [IV] Graf von Wolfratshausen, son of OTTO [III]
2 CONC  von Diessen Graf von Wolfratshausen & his wife Lauritta --- (-killed in battle Pavia 10 Nov 1136).
