2 CONT Otto
2 CONT Father	Otto I Wittelsbach, Duke of Bavaria
2 CONT Mother	Agnes of Loon
2 CONT Richardis of Bavaria (1173 in Kelheim – 7 December 1231 in Roermond) was a German noblewoman. She was a daughter of Count Palatine Otto I of Bavaria, who later became the first Wittelsbach Duke of Bavaria, and his wife Agnes of Lo
2 CONC on.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT In 1186, she married Otto I, Count of Guelders. Together, they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry of Guelders (d. 1198). He was betrothed in 1197 to Aleidis, a daughter of Dirk VII, Count of Holland. However, he died in 1198 before the wedding could take place.
2 CONT Gerard III (1185–1229).
2 CONT Adelaide (d. 1218), married William I, Count of Holland.[1]
2 CONT Otto (1193–1213), was Bishop of Utrecht as Otto I
2 CONT Irmgard, married Adolph, Count of Altena and Mark, son of Frederick I, Count of Berg-Altena and his wife Alveradis.
2 CONT Margaret, married Lothar III, Count of Hochstadt
2 CONT Matilda, married Henry II, Count of Nassau.
2 CONT After her husband died in 1207, she became abbess of the Cistercian abbey in Roermond. She died in Roermond in 1231, and was buried in the Church of Our Lady.
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnotes
2 CONT  Johannes de Beke Chronologia 61, p. 141.
2 CONT
