1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Poppo van Henegouwen van Würzburg (van Würzburg), Graf, Burggraf von Würzburg
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221676580142&size=medium}}
2 CONT ''Coat of Arms of the Bisopric of Wurzburg'' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parent house	Popponids (Babenberg) in turn from the Robertians
2 CONT Titles	Princely Counts of Henneberg
2 CONT Estate	County of Henneberg
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221676686921&size=large}}
2 CONT ''County of Henneberg around 1350''
2 CONT In the 11th century, the dynasty's estates around the ancestral seat Henneberg Castle near Meiningen belonged to the German stem duchy of Franconia. They were located southwest of the Rennsteig ridge in the Thuringian Forest, then
2 CONC  forming the border with the possessions held by the Landgraves of Thuringia in the north. In 1096 one Count Godebold II of Henneberg served as a burgrave of the Würzburg bishops, his father Poppo had been killed in battle in 1078
2 CONC . In 1137 he established Verssa Abbey near Hildburghausen as the family's house monastery.
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221677047836&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT …..
2 CONT POPPO [I] (-killed in battle near Melrichstadt 7 Aug 1078).  Graf von Henneberg.  m as her first husband, HILDEGARD, daughter of LUDWIG "Cum-barba" Graf in Thuringia & his wife Cäcilie von Sangerhausen (-bur Goseck).  The Historia
2 CONC  Brevis Principum Thuringiæ names (in order) "Hildegardis…Uta…Adelheidis" as the three daughters of "Ludewicus Cum-barba" & his wife, specifying that Hildegard married firstly "Bopponi comiti de Hennenberc" and secondly "Timoni de
2 CONC  Nordeke"[68].  She married secondly Thiemo von Nordeck.  Graf Poppo [I] & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT Source: Cawley, Charles. “THURINGIAN NOBILITY.” Fmg.ac, 2025, fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/THURINGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#PoppoIHennebergdied1078. Accessed 11 Oct. 2025.
2 CONT
2 CONT Poppo married Hildegard VON THÜRINGEN, daughter of Ludwig "der Bärtiger" VON THÜRINGEN Count of Thuringia and Gfn. Cäcilie VON SANGERHAUSEN. (Hildegard VON THÜRINGEN was born about 1045 in Thuringia.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Curator Note: Medlands shows only two sons, Poppo II and Gotebold II, no daughters…
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221666120191&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221666215059&size=large}}
2 CONT
