1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Henegouwen" is the Dutch name for the historical region and present-day province of Hainaut in Belgium. It is a geographical term, and surnames that include "van Henegouwen" mean "from Hainaut" and indicate a fami
2 CONC ly's origin in this area.  Hainaut (Henegouwen) is a province in the southern part of Belgium. It was also a historical county within the medieval Holy Roman Empire.  The word is a Dutch toponym, a name referring to a place. It of
2 CONC ten appears in Dutch and Flemish surnames, such as "van Henegouwen," which identifies the origin of a family line.
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221666291882&size=large}}
2 CONT ''Flanders and Hainault''
2 CONT
2 CONT The early arms of Henegouwen are attributed to the County of Hainaut, later to become the House of Avenes, counts of Hainaut after 1314.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina van Henegouwen, born in Henneberg in 1065 (1), died in Kleve in 1100 (2), daughter of Poppo van Henegouwen van Würzburg and Hildegard van Schauenburg, marries (3) with Dirck van Bemmel, born in Kleve in 1050, (4) died in
2 CONC  Kleve in 1096 (5), from the marriage with Dirck van Bemmel:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia van Bemmel, born in Bemmel in 1090 (6), died * 1138, marries * 3 children with Godfried II van Rhenen, born * 1082, 3 died in Utrecht on May 27, 1178 (7)
2 CONT
2 CONT vader
