2 CONT 1255 - 120 Count Diether of Katzenelnbogen belongs to the Rhine Country Peace Alliance -  Rhenish League 
2 CONT                                                                See Weiland, constitute. II, 428 VI Google search: TjT notes: The Rhenish League was a short-lived (1254-7) confederation of Rhineland towns which begain in Mainz and 
2 CONC Worms. The league was founded and administered by Wolpode Arnold so as to secure the law and order in the face of a breakdown of central power and to protect property, commerce, trade and  the rights of the estates.      http://ww
2 CONC w.san.beck.org/7-4-GermanEmpire.html
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1247 a citizen of Mainz called Arnold of the Tower had organized a movement against the heavy tolls on the Rhine and other exactions and robberies by the nobles which led to forming the Rhenish League. The archbishops, bishops,
2 CONC  and nobles from Mainz, Cologne, Worms, Speyer, Strasbourg, Basel, and Metz gained more independence and formed a public peace treaty that spread in 1255 to the Rhineland, Westphalia, and to southern and northern Germany. When Jew
2 CONC s of Halle were persecuted by Archbishop Ruprecht von Magdeburg in 1261, citizens protected them. Citizens of Wurzburg forced Bishop Tring to lift the interdict in 1265 and defeated his successor Berthold in a battle at Kitzingen 
2 CONC in 1269. The citizens of Augsburg defeated Bishop Hartmann. By 1271 the League had sixty Rhenish and Swabian towns and had overcome several robber knights.
2 CONT
2 CONT Founded in 1254, after only two years the league included over 70 cities from Lübeck in the north to Zurich in the south. Many lay and ecclesiastical princes also joined the league and it was recognized by William, Count of Hollan
2 CONC d in 1255. However, following the disputed elections of 1257 it disintegrated and was finally dissolved in 1257. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1256 121 injured by Count Diether Katzenelnbogen against the citizens of Mainz and the Rhine country of peace is besieged by then 26 cities of the Rhine country supposedly peace in federal Rheinfels. The siege lasted a year and 14
2 CONC  weeks and cost only to the citizens of Worms 2000 Mk; still could not take the federal government Rheinfels.
2 CONT                 Ann. Wormatienses a.a. 1256
2 CONT
2 CONT Mainz, August 16 1258 128 King Richard declares that his side out of the Count Diether of Katzenelnbogen (Catsenellenboghe) that he has taken the Archbishop Gerhard von Mainz Dhaun caught and imprisoned, no harm or discomfort will
2 CONC  be added. - Sg of Exh. - D. Maguntie XVI indiction prima augusti 1258, regni vero nostri anno secundo.
2 CONT                 StA Ausf. Marburg, Katzenelnbogen. From Sg.
2 CONT
