1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.geni.com/people/Dietrich-I-count-in-the-Hassegau/6000000002187684590?through=6000000047766418840 DIETRICH] [Theoderic], son of --- (-before 976).  [Graf im Hassegau].  The Annalista Saxo calls him "The
2 CONC odericus egregie libertatis vir" and names his two sons[248].  "Otto…rex" confirmed previous grants to Kloster Gandersheim including property "in pago Suththuringa in comitatu Uuillihelmi…[et] in pago Nordthuringa…in comitatu Theo
2 CONC derici in loco…Uuanzleua…[et] in Hliuthirithi in comitatu Irmenfridi" by charter dated 21 Apr 956[249].  "Otto…imperator augustus" donated property "in pagis Derlingon et Nortduringen in comitatu ipsius Mamaconi" to "nostro fideli
2 CONC  Mamaconi" at the request of "Theoderici comitis" by charter dated 23 Apr 966[250]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m [https://www.geni.com/people/Imma/6000000004543860129 IMMA], daughter of ---.  976.  "Otto…imperator augustus" confirmed donations of property "in Livbedinga in pago Gurketal et in comitatu Ratoldi comitis" by "Theoderici comiti
2 CONC s cuidam viduæ Imma" for the foundation of a monastery by charter dated 11 Jun 975[251], although it is not known whether this refers to the same Graf Dietrich.  Thietmar records that Dedo "went so far as to capture his own mother
2 CONC " when leading "the rebellious Bohemians against us at the church of Zeitz"[252]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Dietrich & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Dedi-I-von-Wettin-margrave-of-Merseburg/6000000003858812164?through=6000000002187684590 DEDO] [I] (-killed in battle near Mose bei Wolmirstedt 13 Nov 1009).  He is named as son of Dietrich 
2 CONC in the Annalista Saxo, which records that he served Markgraf Ricdag and his son Karl[253].  Thietmar records that he was appointed Graf von Merseburg in succession to Count Bio[254].  m (before 985) [https://www.geni.com/people/Th
2 CONC ietburga-von-Haldensleben/6000000003318546921?through=6000000003858812164 THIETBURGA] [von Haldensleben], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Dietrich-von-Haldensleben-margrave-of-the-Saxon-Nordmark/6000000003318525381?throug
2 CONC h=6000000003318546921 DIETRICH] Markgraf über den Gau der Heveller [Nordmark] & his wife ---.  The parentage of the wife of Graf Dedo is deduced from her brother Bernhard being described as avunculus of her son, although she is no
2 CONC t named in this passage[255].  Thietmar is more explicit, stating that Dedo married "Markgraf Dietrich's daughter, Thiedburga"[256].  Graf Dedo [I] & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Dietric-II-von-Wettin-margrave-of-the-Saxon-Ostmark/6000000002204465217?through=6000000003858812164 DIETRICH] (-murdered 19 Nov 1034).  "Theoderico, Dedonis occisi filio" is named in the A
2 CONC nnalista Saxo, when recording that the king installed him in his father's Grafschaft[257].  Graf in Eilenburg 1017.  Graf im Hassegau und Siusli 1021.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>m [https://www.geni.com/people/Mathilde-of-Meissen/6000000003827305841?through=6000000002204465217 MATHILDE von Meissen], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Eckhard-I-von-Merseburg-Count-of-Merseberg-Margrave-of-Meissen/60
2 CONC 00000001354491504?through=6000000003827305841 EKKEHARD] I Markgraf von Meissen & his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Swanhilde-of-Saxony/6000000002187651872?through=6000000003827305841 Schwanehild] [Billung].  The Chronicon Mont
2 CONC is Serreni names "Machtildem" as daughter of "Ekkehardo marchioni" & his wife and names her husband "Tidericus comes"[266]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Graf Dietrich & his wife had seven children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Friedrich-von-Munster-bishop/6000000002187656168  '''FRIEDRICH'''] (-Münster 18 Apr 1084, bur Münster Cathedral).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "filios: Fridericum, Dedonem, Thiemone
2 CONC m, Geronem, Conradum, Riddagum, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus", specifying that "primus filius Fridericus fuit prepositus maioris Magdeburgensis ecclesie, postea Monasteriensis episcopus"[267].  Provost at Magd
2 CONC eburg cathedral before 1063.  Elected Bishop of Magdeburg 1063.  Provost of Münster cathedral 1063.  Imperial chancellor.  Bishop of Münster 1064.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Dedi-I-Margrave-of-the-Saxon-Ostmark/6000000003495414717?through=6000000002187656168 DEDO] [II] (-Oct 1075).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "filios: Fridericum, Dedonem, Thiemonem, Ge
2 CONC ronem, Conradum, Riddagum, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus", specifying that "secundus filius Dedo obtinuit marchiam Hodonis marchionis, qui heredem non habuit"[268].  Graf im Gau Siusli 1043.  Markgraf der Niede
2 CONC rlausitz 1046.  Graf im südliche Schwabengau [1046/68]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>3.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Thiemo-II-Graf-von-Wettin/6000000004533699347?through=6000000003495414717  THIMO] (-after [1099/1101]).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "filios: Fridericum, Dedonem, Thiemonem, Geronem
2 CONC , Conradum, Riddagum, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus"[269].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>4.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gero-von-Wettin/6000000002187656162?through=6000000004533699347  GERO] (-after 1089).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "filios: Fridericum, Dedonem, Thiemonem, Geronem, Conradum, Riddag
2 CONC um, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus"[270].  Graf von Brehna.  m as her second husband, BERTA ---, widow of POPPO von Wippra, daughter of --- (-17 Sep, 1089 or before).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Bertam v
2 CONC iduam cuiusdam Popponis" as wife of "quartus filius [comitis Tiderici] Gero comes", specifying that "huius Popponis frater fuit Cuno senior de Wippera"[271].  "Heinricus…Romanorum imperator augustus" confirmed a donation to the ch
2 CONC urch of Naumburg by "domne Berthe fuit uxoris…comitis Geronis" to Naumburg church by charter dated 12 Dec 1089, which names "fidelium nostrorum Geronis comitis, Guntheri episcopi, Theoderici et Willihelmi filiorum suorum"[272], th
2 CONC e charter being marked spurious in the compilation although the genealogical information in the document is corroborated by other sources.  Graf Gero & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>a)         DIETRICH (-14 Oct [1089/1115], bur Naumburg Cathedral).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Tidericum comitem et Willehelmum comitem de Canburch et Guntherum Cicensem episcopum" as the three sons of "quartus filius 
2 CONC [comitis Tiderici] Gero comes" & his wife[273].  Graf von Brehna.  m GERBURG, daughter of --- (-21 Oct -, bur Naumburg Cathedral).  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>b)         WILHELM (-7 Mar [1089/1115], bur Naumburg Cathedral).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Tidericum comitem et Willehelmum comitem de Canburch et Guntherum Cicensem episcopum" as the three sons of "quartus filius [c
2 CONC omitis Tiderici] Gero comes" & his wife[274].  The Liber de Bello Saxonico records that "Willehelmus, Geronis comitis filius" was captured "ab Everhardo"[275].  Graf von Camburg.  m GEVA Gräfin von Seeburg, daughter of --- (-14 Ma
2 CONC r -, bur Naumburg Cathedral).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   Wilhelm & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>i)          GEVA .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>ii)         BERTA ([1075]-before [1152/56]).  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  Her name is confirmed by the charter dated to [1149] under which her daughter Hedwig Abbess of Gernro
2 CONC de donated part of her inheritance from "matris…eius Berchte et fratris eius comitis Geronis" to Gernrode[276].  m ([1096]) as his second wife, WICHMANN [I] Graf von Seeburg, son of Graf CRISTIN [Querfurt] & his wife Oda von Halde
2 CONC nsleben (-[1115]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>c)         GÜNTHER (-1 Apr 1089, bur Naumburg Cathedral).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Tidericum comitem et Willehelmum comitem de Canburch et Guntherum Cicensem episcopum" as the three sons of "quartus filius [comitis 
2 CONC Tiderici] Gero comes" & his wife[277].  Bishop of Naumburg 1079.  "Heinricus…Romanorum imperator augustus" granted property "quod Gero pater…Gunteri episcopi dederat in comitatu Hasgethe Friderici palatini comiti et in pago Helfet
2 CONC he et in Scafestede" to Naumburg church by charter dated 10 Aug 1088, at the request of "Ekkeberti marchionis, Heinrici marchionis…Gunteri Nuienburgensis sedis episcopi"[278]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>d)         WILLA .  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Willam abbatissam de Gerbestide et Thieburgam prepositam de Gernrode" as the daughters of "quartus filius [comitis Tiderici] Gero comes" & his wife[279].  Abbess of Gerbst
2 CONC edt. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>e)         THIETBURG .  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Willam abbatissam de Gerbestide et Thieburgam prepositam de Gernrode" as the daughters of "quartus filius [comitis Tiderici] Gero comes" & his wife[280].  Nun at Gernr
2 CONC ode.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>5.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Konrad-Landgraf-von-Landsberg-Wettin-Camburg/6000000002187656144?through=6000000002187656162  KONRAD] (-17 Jan or 14 Feb after 1040).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "filios: Fridericu
2 CONC m, Dedonem, Thiemonem, Geronem, Conradum, Riddagum, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus"[281].  Graf von Wettin.  m OTHILDIS von Katlenburg, daughter of DIETRICH [I] Graf von Katlenburg [Stade] & his wife Bertrada of
2 CONC  Holland.  The Annalista Saxo names "Theodericus et…Othilhildis" as children of Graf Dietrich [I] & his wife, specifying that the latter married "Conrado fratri Dedonis marchionis"[282].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "sororem
2 CONC  Tiderici senioris de Kathelenburc…Othilhildis" as wife of "quintus filius [comitis Tiderici] Conradus comes"[283].  Konrad & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>a)         BERTRADA (-1145).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Bertradam" as the daughter of "quintus filius [comitis Tiderici] Conradus comes" & his wife, naming her husband "Beringerus comes frater Ludowici comitis seniori
2 CONC s de Thuringia"[284].  “Comes Ludowicus cum nepote suo Conrado comitis...Berngeri filio...cum uxore eiusdem domini Ludowici Adilheida ac filiis eorundem Hermanno, Ludowico, Heinrico, Conrado, dominaque Berchtrada comitis Conradi m
2 CONC atre” donated “ecclesiam...Sangershusen” to Reinhardsbrunn by charter dated 25 Jul 1110[285].  m BERENGAR Graf von Sangerhausen, son of LUDWIG "mit dem Barten" Graf in Thuringia & his wife Caecilie von Sangerhausen (-before 25 Jul
2 CONC  1110).
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>6.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Rikdag-von-Eilenburg-Wettin/6000000008477713438?through=6000000002187656144  RIKDAG] .  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "filios: Fridericum, Dedonem, Thiemonem, Geronem, Conradum, Ridda
2 CONC gum, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus", specifying that "Riddagus sextus filius" died childless[286]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>7.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Hidda-Ida-von-Wettin-Duchess-of-Bohemia/6000000002187656156?through=6000000008477713438  HIDDA] von Eilenburg .  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "filios: Fridericum, Dedonem, Thiemonem,
2 CONC  Geronem, Conradum, Riddagum, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus", specifying that Hidda married "duci Boemico"[287].  m SPYTIHNĔV II Duke of the Bohemians, son of BŘETISLAV Duke of the Bohemians & his wife Judith v
2 CONC on Schweinfurt (1031-28 Jan 1061). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Friedrich-von-Wettin-und-Eilenburg-graf/6000000002187656214?through=6000000002187684590 FRIEDRICH von Eilenburg] (-Eilenburg 6 Jan 1017).  "Dedonem et Fridericum" are named as sons of Dietr
2 CONC ich in the Annalista Saxo[258].  Burggraf von Meissen.  Herr von Eilenburg.  Thietmar records the death of "Count Friedrich…in his burg Eilenburg", stating that he transferred Eilenburg to "his brother's son Dietrich" before he di
2 CONC ed while it was agreed that his remaining lands "would pass to his three daughters"[259].  The Genealogica Wettinensis records his death "in eadem civitate [=Hileburc civitatem suam] in sacra nocte epiphanie Domini"[260].  m ---. 
2 CONC  The name of Friedrich's wife is not known.  Graf Friedrich & his wife had three daughters.  
