2 CONC ame source.   This is impossible chronologically as the children of Markgraf Dedo must have been born after 1039, the earliest date of his marriage, while Friedrich von Goseck died in [1042].  The Chronicon Gozecense apparently id
2 CONC entifies the correct origin of Agnes, wife of Friedrich von Goseck, when it names "Oudam" as daughter of "comes Fridericus [et] Agnam…de Wimare"[319], the latter being the sister of Oda der Ostmark's first husband Wilhelm [III] Gr
2 CONC af von Weimar (see THURINGIAN NOBILITY).  The question remains whether these sources should be interpreted broadly as meaning that Markgraf Dedo [II] did have a second daughter named Agnes by his first marriage and that she was ma
2 CONC rried to another individual named Friedrich.  m FRIEDRICH "Graf in Sachsen".] 
