2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nikon chronicle under the year 1147 reports that "... Prince Andrey Rostislavich came from Ryazan and of Yelets to the Davydovich in Chernigov", who fought at that time against the Grand Duke of Kyiv Izyaslav Mstislavich.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Rostislav Yaroslavich - prince of Pronsk, Ryazan and Murom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brothers:
2 CONT * Gleb (died 1177) - Prince of Ryazan (1145-1177 intermittently).
2 CONT * Yuri (L. Voitovich identifies him with Andrey as the same person, in this case, Andrey had a son and a daughter, presumably married to Oleg Svyatoslavich of Chernigov).
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrey Rostislavich left no offspring, no issue.
