1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1218, Yaroslav married his third wife Fedosia Igorevich of Ryazan. She was the daughter of Igor Glebovich and Agrafena of Kiev. Her father was the second son of Gleb Rostislavich, Prince of Ryazan (d. 1178) and 
2 CONC Euphrosyne of Pereyaslavl. Her mother was the daughter of Rostislav I of Kiev. They had at least twelve children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Fyodor Yaroslavich (Winter, 1219 - 5 June 1233). Betrothed to Euphrosyne Mikhailovna of Chernigov. She was a daughter of Michael of Chernigov and Maria Romanovna of Galicia and Volynia. Fyodor died the day before his marriage da
2 CONC te.
2 CONT # Alexander Nevsky (30 May 1220 - 14 November 1263).
2 CONT # Andrei II of Vladimir (c. 1222–1264).
2 CONT # Mikhail Khorobrit, Prince of Moscow. Took control of Vladimir and proclaimed himself its Prince in 1248. Killed while facing a Lithuanian invasion.
2 CONT # Daniil Yaroslavich (d. 1256).
2 CONT # Yaroslav of Tver (d. 9 September 1271).
2 CONT # Konstantin Yaroslavich, Prince of Galich and Dmitrov.
2 CONT # Maria Yaroslavna (born 1240).
2 CONT # Vasily of Kostroma (1241–1276).
2 CONT # Afanasy Yaroslavich.
2 CONT # Eudoxia Yaroslavna.
2 CONT # Iuliana Yaroslavna.
