1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Grand Duke of Kiev Mstislav==
2 CONT
2 CONT Mstislav Romanovich the Old (Мстислав Романович Старый in Russian) (? - 1223), Prince of Pskov (1179 - ?), Smolensk (1197 - ?), Belgorod (1206), Halych (? - ?) and Grand Prince of Kiev (1212-1223). Son of Roman Rostislavich.
2 CONT Mstislav went to war against the Mongols of Genghis Khan in 1223 and was defeated at the Battle of the Kalka River by the Mongol generals, Jebe and Subutai, after which he was executed by suffocation (put under a giant wooden plat
2 CONC e onto which Subutai, Jebe and other Mongol warlords danced and feasted).
2 CONT ( http://www.geni.com/people/Genghis-Khan-Tem%C3%BCjin-Khagan-of-the-Mongol-Empire/375784306260002721 ).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Family of MSTISLAV Romanovich "Dobriy/the Good"
2 CONT
2 CONT ROMAN Rostislavich, son of ROSTISLAV Mstislavich Grand Prince of Kiev & his wife --- (-14 Jun 1180).  Prince of Smolensk 1159-1172, 1177-1180.  He succeeded as ROMAN Grand Prince of Kiev 1172-1174, 1175-1177.  Prince of Novgorod 1
2 CONC 154, 1178-1179. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (9 Jan 1149) as her first husband, MARIA Sviatoslavna, daughter of SVIATOSLAV NIKOLAI Olegovich Prince of Chernigov & his second wife Maria [Ekaterina] of Novgorod.  She married secondly Roman Glebovich Prince of Riazan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Prince Roman & his wife had three children (all of whom, along with their descendants shown below, are named by Baumgarten with primary sources[541]):
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         IAROPOLK Romanovich (-after 1176).  Prince of Smolensk 1172-1174.  m ---.  The name of Iaropolk´s wife is not known.  Iaroolk & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         [VISLAVA Iaropolkovna .  Baumgarten quotes an early secondary source which names "Wislawa fil. Jarolphi Principis Russiæ" as the wife of Duke Bogislaw, suggesting that "Jarolphi" is a corruption of "Jaropolk", and sugge
2 CONC sts three possible contemporary Princes Iaropolk[542].  He dismisses Iaropolk Prince of Buzsk on the basis that any of his daughters would have been too old, and Iaropolk of Suzdal on the basis that his branch contracted no known 
2 CONC western marriages as they had orientated themselves towards Byzantium, leaving only Iaropolk Romanovich Prince of Smolensk.  m as his first wife, BOGISLAW II Duke of Pomerania, son of BOGISLAW I Duke of Pomerania & his second wife
2 CONC  Anastasia of Poland (-24 Jan 1220).]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         --- Romanovna.  m VSESLAV II Vasilkovich Prince of Polotsk, son of VASILKO Sviatoslavich Prince of Polotsk & his wife --- (-1186]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         MSTISLAV Romanovich "Dobriy/the Good" (-killed in battle Kalka River 30 May 1223).  Prince of Pskov 1178-1195.  Prince of Smolensk 1197-1213.  He succeeded in 1214 as MSTISLAV Grand Prince of Kiev.  He was captured and 
2 CONC killed by the Mongols during their first wave of invasions into Rus territory.  m --- Vasilkovna, daughter of VASILKO Bryacheslavich Prince of Vitebsk & his wife --- Davidovna of Novgorod and Smolensk.  Mstislav & his wife had sev
2 CONC en children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         SVIATOSLAV Mstislavich.  Prince of Novgorod 1218-1219.  Prince of Polotsk 1222-1232.  Prince of Smolensk 1232-1239.  SVIATOSLAV Grand Prince of Kiev 1235. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         IZIASLAV Mstislavich.  IZIASLAV IV Grand Prince of Kiev 1235.  Prince of Smolensk 1239. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         VSEVOLOD Mstislavich (-[1238/39]).  Prince of Pskov 1214.  Prince of Novgorod 1219-1221.  Prince of Smolensk 1238. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         ROSTISLAV Mstislavich.  He claimed the vacant throne of Kiev after Mikhail Vsevolodich fled to Hungary in the face of the Mongol invasion, succeeding in 1239 as ROSTISLAV III Grand Prince of Kiev.  He was expelled in hi
2 CONC s turn by Daniil Romanovich Prince of Volynia[543].    
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         ANDREI Mstislavich (-killed in battle 1245). 
2 CONT
2 CONT f)          --- Mstislavna.  m ANDREI Prince of --- (-killed in battle 1223).  
2 CONT
2 CONT g)         --- Mstislavna (-24 Jan 1221 or [1222]).  m (15 Oct 1195) KONSTANTIN Vsevolodich Grand Prince of Vladimir, son of VSEVOLOD Iurievich "Balshoe Gniezdo/Big Nest" Prince of Vladimir & his first wife Maria of Ossetia (-2 Fe
2 CONC b 1218).
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Mstislav Romanovitch  - Mstislav III Boris de Kiev   :__:  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kievan_Rus%27#mediaviewer/File:Kingdom_of_Galicia_Volhynia_Rus%27_Ukraine_1245_1349.jpg
2 CONT
