2 CONT
2 CONT By his marriage to Euphrosyne Doucaena Camaterina Alexios had three daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Eirene Angelina''', who married 
2 CONT # Andronicus Contostephanus, and 
2 CONT # Alexius Palaeologus, by whom she was the grandmother of Emperor Michael VIII Palaeologus.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2010571204.htm#EireneAdiedafter1203
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''EIRENE Komnene Angelina''' (-after 1203).  Niketas Choniates names "Contostephanus Andronicus et Isaacius Comenus" as "duo generi" of Emperor Alexios[776].  Ephræmius records that "filiarum…Irene natu maior" married 
2 CONC "Andronico…de Contostephanis"[777].  Niketas Choniates records the second marriage of "imperator…filias…Irenem" and "Alexio Paleologo"[778].  Georgius Akropolites records that "Palaeologo, qui despotæ dignitate…" married "imperato
2 CONC ris Alexii…filiarum illius…prima Irene"[779].  She went into exile in 1203.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly as his second wife, ANDRONIKOS Kontostefanos, son of STEFANOS Kontostefanos, panhypersébastos, megas doux & his wife Anna Komnene (-[1196]).  Mega drongarios.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (1199) as his second wife, ALEXIOS Komnenos Palaiologos, son of --- Doukas Palaiologos & his wife Eirene Komnene Kantakouzene (-[1201/04]).  He was awarded the title despot in 1199. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
