1 OCCU Comte, de Berg-Schalkingen, Greve av Berg-Schelklingen, Graf, stirbt als Mönch; Busse, DFA57. H. 1., Graf v.Berg um 1100, Mönch in Zwiefalten; v.Damm, Count of Berg-Schelklingen, Greve
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Heinrich Graf von Berg-Schelklingen''' was born circa 1073 in Schelklingen, Alb-Donau-Kreis, Baden-Württemberg, Germany. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-38474969 Poppo (1055~1090) Graf von Roggenstein und Berg] a
2 CONC nd [https://www.geni.com/profile-119505100 ÁRPÁD(házi) Sophia]. He was a Comte, de Berg-Schalkingen, Greve av Berg-Schelklingen, Graf, stirbt als Mönch; Busse, DFA57. H. 1., Graf v.Berg um 1100, Mönch in Zwiefalten; v.Damm, Count 
2 CONC of Berg-Schelklingen, Greve. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich married [https://www.geni.com/profile-26735094 Adelheid von Vohburg] in 1083. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-1792247 Salomea* von Berg-Schelklingen]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-21724124 Richza von Berg-Schelklingen]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-38476987 Diepold I von Berg-Schelklingen]; [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/profile-63353869 S Berg Schelkingen]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-81025679 Sophie von Berg- Schelklingen]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died circa September 24, 1122 in Zwiefalten, Reutlingen, Baden-Württemberg, Germany. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT *http://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I26491&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Berg-446 ''(abt. 1073 - bef. 1116)''
2 CONT --------
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WURTTEMBERG.htm#HeinrichBergdiedbefore1116<br/>
2 CONT a)         HEINRICH [I] (-Zwiefalten 24 Sep before 1116, bur Zwiefalten).  Ortlieb's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names "Heinricus de Berge" as son of "Bobbonis comitis et Sophiæ ipsius uxori"[206].  Graf von Berg.  He became a monk at
2 CONC  Zwiefalten.  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "VIII Kal Oct" of "Heinricus com senior de Berge…sepultus in Capitolio...cum patre suo Poppone et fratribus suis" and his donation of “curiam Oppinthal”[207].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ADELHEID von Mochental, daughter of [DIEPOLD [II] von Giengen Markgraf im Nordgau & his wife Liutgarde von Zähringen] (-1 Dec [1125]).  The primary source which confirms her precise parentage has not yet been identified, a
2 CONC lthough the following necrology entry indicates her possible family origin.  It is, however, unusual for a deceased married lady to be referred to in contemporary necrologies with a comital title derived from her birth family.  It
2 CONC  is therefore possible that the reference to “Mochental” relates to an otherwise unrecorded second husband.  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "Kal Dec" of "Adelheit com de Mochintal et c v, mater Salome ducisse"[208].
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT  Heinrich & his wife had six children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://books.google.fi/books?id=cUdSAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA303&lpg=PA303&dq=Poppo+Graf+von+Berg-Schelklingen&source=bl&ots=QroVtqxfhl&sig=ux9felQGNk1nzmPYYPiT6pZml5g&hl=fi&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiLsq6Hp9zOAhWBO5oKHXmzBLw4FBDoAQgmMAE#v=onepage&q=
2 CONC Poppo%20Graf%20von%20Berg-Schelklingen&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT  s p a m 
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWABIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#PoppoBergMSophie
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''POPPO''' (-11 Jul <nowiki>----</nowiki>, bur ---, transferred to Zwiefalten).  Graf von Berg.  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "V Id Jul" of "Bobbo com de Berge, pater Hainrici senioris comitis de Berge
2 CONC "[1136].  m SOPHIE, daughter of --- (-26 Jun [1110], bur ---, transferred to Zwiefalten).  Ortlieb's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names "Bobbonis comitis et Sophiæ ipsius uxori", when recording that their son Heinrich transferred their
2 CONC  remains to Zwiefalten[1137].  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "VI Kal Jul" of "Sophia com de Berge"[1138].  Europäische Stammtafeln[1139] shows Sophia, wife of Graf Poppo, as Sophia of Hungary, daughter of Salomon K
2 CONC ing of Hungary.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Poppo & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''HEINRICH (-Zwiefalten 24 Sep before 1116, bur Zwiefalten)'''.  Ortlieb's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names "Heinricus de Berge" as son of "Bobbonis comitis et Sophiæ ipsius uxori"[1140].  Graf von Berg.  He became a monk
2 CONC  at Zwiefalten.  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "VIII Kal Oct" of "Heinricus com senior de Berge…sepultus in Capitolio" and his donation "cum patre suo Poppone et fratribus suis"[1141].  m ADELHEID von Mochental, da
2 CONC ughter of [DIEPOLD [II] von Giengen Markgraf im Nordgau & his wife Liutgarde von Zähringen] (-1 Dec [1125]).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  The necrology of Zwiefalten r
2 CONC ecords the death "Kal Dec" of "Adelheit com de Mochintal et c v, mater Salome ducisse"[1142].  It is unusual for a deceased married noble lady to be referred to by her unmarried title in the necrologies.  It is possible that "von 
2 CONC Mochental" was the name of a second husband.  Graf Heinrich & his wife had six children:  i)          HEINRICH [II] (-24 Feb before 1127, bur Zwiefalten).  Berthold's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names "Heinricus comes" as son of "Hein
2 CONC ricus senior comes de Monte"[1143].  Graf von Berg.  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "VI Kal Mar" of "Heinricus n c m com iunior de Berge…huius sorores Salome ducissa, Richinza ducissa et Sophia ducissa"[1144].  m [B
2 CONC ERTHA von Boll].  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  ii)         DIEPOLD [II] (-19 May [1160/65]).  His parentage is confirmed by the Translatio Manus sancti Stephani which names "Salome u
2 CONC xor [Bolezlai Bolionorum ducis] filia Heinrici comitis de Berge sororque Diepoldi"[1145].  Graf von Berg.  -         see below.  iii)        RAPOTO (-25 Jun after 1163).  Berthold's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names "Rapto eius alter 
2 CONC filius [=Heinricus senior comes de Monte]"[1146].  "…Comes Diepoldus de Berge ac frater suus Rapado…" witnessed the charter dated 14 Oct 1139 under which Konrad III King of Germany granted protection to the church of Denkendorf[11
2 CONC 47].  The History of Salem Monastery lists those present at a court of "duce Friderico", including "Diepoldo et fratre eius Rapotone comitibus de Berge", undated but dateable to [1152][1148].  Graf von Berg.  "Sex comites…comes Di
2 CONC epoldus et frater suus Rappoto…" witnessed the charter dated 1163 under which Ulrich Abbot of Reichenau confirmed donations to the abbey[1149].  According to Europäische Stammtafeln, he was possible ancestor of the Grafen von Wart
2 CONC stein[1150].  m [UODILHILT Gräfin von Wartstein, daughter of --- (-29 Mar <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  The primary source which confirms her origin and marriage has not yet been identified.] iv)       SALOME (before 1101-27 Jul 1144).
2 CONC   The Chronica Boemorum names "Almuse" as wife of "dux Bolezlaus"[1151].  Berthold's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names (in order) "Richinza ductrix Boemiæ, Sophia ductrix Moraviæ, Salome ductrix Poloniæ" as sisters of "Heinricus comes
2 CONC  [et] Rapot", specifying that Salome was "uxor Bolezlaus dux Boloniæ"[1152].  The Chronica principum Polonie records that the second wife of "Boleslaus" was "ex Theutunica"[1153].  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "VI
2 CONC  Kal 1144" of "Salome ducisse Bolonie"[1154].  m ([Mar/Jul] 1115) as his second wife, BOLESŁAW III "Krzywousty/Wrymouth" Duke of Poland, son of WŁADYSŁAW I HERMAN Prince of Poland & his second wife Judith of Bohemia (20 Aug [1086]
2 CONC -28 Oct 1138).  v)        RICHINZA (-27 Sep 1125).  Berthold's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names (in order) "Richinza ductrix Boemiæ, Sophia ductrix Moraviæ, Salome ductrix Poloniæ" as sisters of "Heinricus comes [et] Rapot", specifyi
2 CONC ng in the subsequent paragraph that Richinza was "uxor Vlatizlaus qui et Lauzlan dux Boemiæ"[1155].  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "V Kal Oct" of "Richinza ductrix Boemie filie Heinrici comitis senioris"[1156].  m 
2 CONC ([1110]) VLADISLAV I Duke of the Bohemians, son of VRATISLAV II Duke of the Bohemians & his third wife Swiętoslawa [Svatana] of Poland (-12 Apr 1125, bur Prague St Maria).  vi)       SOPHIE (-31 May [1126]).  Berthold's Chronicon 
2 CONC of Zwiefalten names (in order) "Richinza ductrix Boemiæ, Sophia ductrix Moraviæ, Salome ductrix Poloniæ" as sisters of "Heinricus comes [et] Rapot", specifying in the subsequent paragraph that Sophia was "uxor Ottonis ducis"[1157]
2 CONC .  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "II Kal Jun" of "Sophia cv et ductrix Moravie, soror Salome ducisse"[1158].  m (after 1113) OTTO II "Niger" Duke of Moravia in Olmütz und Brünn, son of OTTO I "der Schöne" Duke of M
2 CONC oravia in Olmütz and Brno & his wife Ludmilla [Euphemia] of Hungary (-28 Feb 1126).
