1 NOTE The dynasty of Jagello who ruled Poland and Lithuania began in 1386. The Jagello Dynasty ruled until 1572.  The family also ruled Lithuania and Bohemia.  Under the jagello rulers the Poles and Lithuanians won joint victories over 
2 CONC the Teutonic Knights (1410-1466) and found against the expanding power of Muscovite Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his marriage to Jadwiga, Queen of Poland, the Lithuanian Jogaillo, Grand Duke of Lithuania, became converted to Christianity, and thus brought about the Christian conversion of Lithuania and the eventual union of Poland with 
2 CONC Lithuania.
