1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Swalgote''', born ca 1280, the Duke of Lithuania. A son of the Grand Duke of Lithuania Vytenis.
2 CONT In 1309, a large Lithuanian army marched to Livonia, which made it easier for Vytenis to attack it in 1310 - the vassal castle of the Archbishop of Riga, Lielstraupė (Latvia), was besieged.
2 CONT After his father's death (1316), Swalgote did not take part in the struggle for the throne of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, so it is believed that he died earlier, ca. August 1342. Prince of Polotzk (1307- 1316, 1326–1342). (infor
2 CONC mations from genealogy Gedyminas- Galitzine). 
