1 NOTE {geni:about_me} a)         [604][INGERD [Ingeborg] (-before 1236).  "M[yroszlava] et Hyn[gardis]…ductrices Slavie…cum filiis nostris et ducibus Barnym et Wartizlao" donated property to Kloster Mogilno in Colberg by charter dated t
2 CONC o [1223/24][605].  Her Danish royal origin is indicated by the charter dated 1225 under which her son "Wartislaus…dux Pomeranorum et Diminensium" donated property to Kloster Dargun, sealed by "ducis Worzlai e sanguine regis Danor"
2 CONC [606].  '''From a chronological point of view, it seems likely that Ingerd was the daughter of King Knud VI: the children of Knud´s brother King Valdemar II were born too late for one of them to have been the mother of Wartislaw D
2 CONC uke of Pomerania, and King Knud´s father, King Valdemar I, is already recorded with a daughter named Ingebjörg.'''  Another possibility is that she was descended from the Danish royal family in the female line.  The date of her ma
2 CONC rriage is estimated assuming that the date of birth of her son Wartislaw is correctly estimated as shown in the document POMERANIA.  "M[yroszlava] et Hyn[gardis]…ductrices Slavie…cum filiis nostris et ducibus Barnym et Wartizlao" 
2 CONC donated property to Kloster Mogilno in Colberg by charter dated to [1223/24][607].  "Anastasia…ducissa Pomeranorum" donated property to Kloster Belbog, with the consent of "dominarum relicte…filii mei Bugzlai et alterius filii Kaz
2 CONC emari relicte" by charter dated 7 Jul 1224 witnessed by "…Barnota filius domini Jaromiri de Ruia…"[608].  "Dominus Barnym…dux Slauorum…et…fratre meo germano domino dice Wartislao" renewed the donations to Kloster Mogilno made by "
2 CONC mater nostra domina Myroslaua…post mortem domini mei Boguslai…[et] mee matertere…Hyngardis domina terre Slauie relicta ducis Kazimari" by charter dated 1236[609].  m (before [1208/10]) KASIMIR II Duke of Pomerania, son of BOGISLAW
2 CONC  I Duke of Pomerania & his second wife Anastasia of Poland ([1180]-before 20 Jun 1219).] 
