2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith of Thuringia
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith of Thuringia (Czech: Judita Durynská, c. 1135 - d. 9 September after 1174) was the second wife of Duke and later King Vladislaus II of Bohemia and since 1158 the second Queen of Bohemia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Vladislaus II
2 CONT
2 CONT Vladislaus married Judith, daughter of Louis I, Landgrave of Thuringia, in 1153, three years after the death of his first wife Gertrude. The main reason was that Judith was related to the new German king Frederick I. Vladislaus' b
2 CONC ride was most probably eighteen, he was 15-20 years older.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Queen Judith
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably in 1155, two years after the wedding, Judith gave birth to the first son. In medieval times the names for babies were chosen mostly by mothers, so it was probably Judith's idea to name the son Přemysl (name of the legenda
2 CONC ry founder of the dynasty)[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT A chronicler wrote about Judith that she was of great beauty and mind, educated in Latin and politics. It is said that she often deputized Vladislaus in his absent. Whe he was crowned in 1158, Judith became the queen. Her coronati
2 CONC on is not actually documented, but chronicles write about Queen Judith.
2 CONT
2 CONT During Vladislaus' rule a new bridge in Prague was built, where the Charles bridge stands today. It was the first stone bridge in central Europe and in honour of the queen it was called Judith's bridge.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Vladislaus abdicated in 1172, his wife followed him to exile. It is not known where she died, but her remains were found in a monastery in the town of Teplice. According to Emanuel Vlček she died as an old lady after 1210, li
2 CONC ving to see successful reign of her eldest son Přemysl[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Ottokar, later king of Bohemia, first of a hereditary line
2 CONT
2 CONT Ladislaus, later duke of Bohemia as Ladislaus III
2 CONT
2 CONT Richeza (died 19 April 1182), married to the son of Henry II, Duke of Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judith_of_Thuringia Her parents are disputed name Ludwig=Louis, Language barrier her husband was Vladislav Premysl II of Bohemia, Mother of Ottokar I the photo is of the Facial reconstruction from the
2 CONC  forensic facial reconstruction artist https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Cicero_Moraes 
