1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 OCT 1120
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sommerschenburg
3 STAE Herzogtum Sachsen
3 CTRY Heiliges Römisches Reich
1 OCCU Pfalzgraf von Sachsen (1065-1120)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://saebi.isgv.de/biografie/Friedrich_I.,_Pfalzgraf_von_Sachsen_(um_1060-1120)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXON%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc359919034
2 CONT
2 CONT ADALBERT [Sevecco] von Sommerschenburg, son of --- . m OUDA [Hilaria] von Goseck, daughter of FRIEDRICH [I] von Goseck Pfalzgraf in Sachsen & his wife Agnes von Weimar (-near Zorbau 1088, bur Goseck).  The Chronicon Gozecense name
2 CONC s "Oudam" daughter of "comes Fridericus [et] Agnam…de Wimare"[460].  ... Adalbert & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT *1.         '''FRIEDRICH [I] von Sommerschenburg (-[18 Oct 1120/1121]).'''  He is named son of "Adalbertus Scucco" & his wife, sister of Pfalzgraf Friedrich, in the Annalista Saxo, which specifies that Friedrich succeeded his mate
2 CONC rnal uncle as Pfalzgraf[463].  Pfalzgraf in Sachsen 1097.  The Chronicon Gozecense names "comes Fridericus palatini de Sumersenburch" as son of "Ouda"[464].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Fridericum comitem palatinum" as son 
2 CONC of "Adelbertus quidam nobilis cognominatus Seveke de Sumerschenburc" & his wife Oda[465].  The documents dated Feb 1111 relating to the coronation of Heinrich V King of Germany as emperor name "Fridericum filium sororis suæ, march
2 CONC ionem Engilbertum, marchionem Thiebaldus, comitem Hermannum, Fridericum palatinum comitem de Saxonia, Berlingarium de Bavaria, Godefridum comitem, Fridericum Saxonum, Albertum cancellarium, Cononem fratri Berengarii, Sigebot de Ba
2 CONC varia, Henricum ducem Carinthie, Bertoldum filium ducis Bertoldi" as the emperor's guarantors[466].  "Fridericum palatinum comitem de Saxonia" signed fifth in the list of lay witnesses who swore for Heinrich V King of Germany at t
2 CONC he time of his coronation as emperor in 1111[467].  Vogt of Kloster Schöningen 1120.  m (after 1106) as her second husband, ADELHEID von Laufen, widow of ADOLF [I] von Hövel [Huwili] Graf von Berg, daughter of HEINRICH Graf von La
2 CONC ufen & his wife Ida von Werl.  The Annalista Saxo names "Adelheidam", gives her parentage, her two husbands, her sons by her first husband and her son "palatinum comitem Fridericum iuniorem" by her second husband[468].  Pfalzgraf 
2 CONC Friedrich [I] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT **a)         FRIEDRICH [II] von Sommerschenburg (-19 May 1162, bur Marienthal).  … m (divorced before 1144) as her first husband, LIUTGARD von Stade, daughter of RUDOLF I von Stade Markgraf der Nordmark & his wife Richgard von Spo
2 CONC nheim (-murdered Winzenburg 30 Jan 1152).  …Pfalzgraf Friedrich [II] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT *** ...
2 CONT **b)         ADELHEID von Sommerschenburg (-before 1180).  …m GOSWIN [III] von Valkenburg und Heinsberg, son of GERHARD von Heinsberg und Valkenburg & his wife Oda von Walbeck (-18 Apr [1167/68]).
