1 NOTE Frederick I of Hapsburg-Austria, son of Albert I, became a rival king to rule Imperial Germany in 1314.  His rival was Ludwig IV of Bavaria. Frederick became known as Frederick III Holy Roman Emperor, and ruled until 1325, leaving
2 CONC  Ludwig to rule alone until 1347.  Their successor was Charles IV of Lumembourg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Frederick of Austria succeeded his father Albert I as Sovereign of the Empire of Austria in 1308.  He ruled until 1330, and was succeeded by Albert II under the Regency of Leopold I.
1 NOTE RIVAL KING OF AUSTRIA 1314-1322
