1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Adelheid von Braunschweig-Lüneburg==
2 CONT
2 CONT * BIRTH:	1244 in Germany
2 CONT * DEATH: June 12, 1274 in St. Elisabethkir, Marburg, Hessen Nassau,Prussia
2 CONT * Marburg, Landkreis Marburg-Biedenkopf, Hessen, Germany
2 CONT * BURIAL: Elisabethkirche Marburg, Landkreis Marburg-Biedenkopf, Hessen, Germany
2 CONT * Adelheid was buried along with one of her young children (possibly the unnamed son) in Elisabethkirche. 
2 CONT * Find A Grave Memorial - https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/115096616/adelheid-von_braunschweig_l_neburg
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Spouse==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Adelheid was the daughter of Otto I, Duke von Braunschweig-Lüneburg and Mathilde von Brandenburg In 1262, she married '''Henry I, Landgrave of Hesse,''' the son of Henry II, Duke of Brabant and Sophie of Thuringia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''They were the parents of four daughters and three sons'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Sophia''' (1264–after 12 August 1331), married 1276 to Count Otto I of Waldeck.
2 CONT * '''Henry the Younger''' (1265–23 August 1298).
2 CONT *''' Matilda''' (1267–after 1332), married in 1283 Count Gottfried of Ziegenhain; after 11 October 1309 Philipp III of Falkenstein-Münzenberg.
2 CONT *''' Adelheid''' (1268–7 December 1315), married 1284 to Count Bertold VII of Henneberg-Schleusingen.  Elisabeth (1269/70–19 February 1293), married ca. 1287 to Count Johann of Sayn 
2 CONT * '''an unnamed son''' (ca. 1270–ca. 1274).
2 CONT * '''Otto''' (ca 1272–17 January 1328).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Royalty Guide - http://www.royaltyguide.nl/countries/germany/M/marburg/elisabethkirche.htm
