0 @N6000000002187757056@ NOTE Gertrude of Merania
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Gertrude of Merania (1185 – September 24, 1213) was the first wife of Andrew II, king of Hungary. She was the daughter of Bertold IV, Duke of Meran. Her sister was Agnes of Merania, a famous beauty, who married King Philippe Augus
1 CONC te of France. Yet another sister was St. Hedwig of Andechs.
1 CONT
1 CONT She and Andrew married before 1203, and she was the mother of his successor Bela IV of Hungary and Saint Elizabeth of Hungary, wife of Louis, landgrave of Thuringia. Gertrude was killed in 1213, by the Hungarian noblemen, who were
1 CONC  jealous over the advancement of her relatives at court. Due to the current political situation most of her murderers remained unpunished during the rule of Andrew II. Only Gertrude's son Béla IV took revenge after elevated to the
1 CONC  throne.
1 CONT
1 CONT She is the main antagonist in Ferenc Erkel's opera, Bánk bán.
0 @N6000000002322315094@ NOTE Four years after Gertrude was murdered, Andrew set off on an ill-fated
1 CONT Crusade to the Holy Land. After his return, the barons forced him to agree to
1 CONT the Golden Bull, which became an important part of the Hungarian
1 CONT constitution, limiting royal rights and prerogatives, confirmed basic rights
1 CONT of small landholders and nobles, guaranteed justice for all, and promised to
1 CONT improve the coinage. Under it, nobles had the right to resist by force any
1 CONT royal decrees.
