0 @N6000000002188113710@ NOTE John III, Burgrave of Nuremberg
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT John III of Nuremberg (ca. 1369–11 June 1420, Plassenburg), Margrave of Brandenburg-Kulmbach from the House of Hohenzollern. He was elder son of Frederick V of Nuremberg and Elisabeth of Meißen.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family and children
1 CONT
1 CONT He was married ca 1381 Margaret of Luxemburg, daughter of Charles IV, Holy Roman Emperor and Elizabeth of Pomerania. They had only daughter, Elisabeth (1391–1429), who married Eberhard III, Count of Württemberg.
1 CONT House of Hohenzollern
