0 @N6000000004533182782@ NOTE Notes for Béla IV King of Hungary:
1 CONT
1 CONT Béla IV Árpád ; King Béla IV of Hungary and Croatia (1235-70)
1 CONT
1 CONT http://www.infoplease.com/ce6/people/A0806818.html
1 CONT
1 CONT Bela IV , 1206-70, king of Hungary (1235-70), son and successor ofAndrew II. He tried to curtail the power of the magnates and set outto recover the crownlands his father had given to supporters.Confronted by the menace of the Mon
1 CONC gol invasion, he sent unheededappeals to Pope Gregory IX and Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II, but hewas crushingly defeated at Mohi on the Sajo River in 1241. Returningafter the withdrawal of the invaders, he repopulated the count
1 CONC ry byinviting foreign colonization. In a battle (1246) with the lastBabenberg duke of Austria, the duke was killed but the Austrians werevictorious. Bela's long struggle with Ottocar II, king of Bohemia, forAustria and Styria ende
1 CONC d (1260) in defeat. His last years weredisturbed by the rebellion of his son, later King Stephen V.
