0 @N6000000002187820963@ NOTE Anna Angelina
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Anna Angelina (c. 1176 - 1212) was a daughter of the Byzantine Emperor Alexios III Angelos and of Euphrosyne Doukaina Kamatera.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her first marriage was to the sebastokrator Isaac Komnenos, a great-nephew of the emperor Manuel I Komnenos. They had one daughter, Theodora Angelina. Soon after Anna's father became emperor, in 1195, Isaac Komnenos was dispatched
1 CONC  to combat the Bulgarian Rebellion. He was captured, became a pawn between rival Bulgarian and Vlach factions, and died in chains.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her second marriage to Theodore Laskaris, eventually emperor of Nicaea, was celebrated in a double wedding in early 1200 (the other couple was Anna's sister Eirene and Alexios Palaiologos). Anna and Theodore had three daughters an
1 CONC d two sons:
1 CONT
1 CONT Erene Laskarina, who married (1) general Andronikos Palaiologos; (2) John III Doukas Vatatzes, emperor of Nicaea 
1 CONT Maria Laskarina, who married King Bela IV of Hungary 
1 CONT Eudokia Laskarina 
1 CONT Nicholas (Nikolaos) Laskaris 
1 CONT John (Ioannes) Laskaris 
1 CONT Anna Angelina
1 CONT Angelos
1 CONT Born: c. 1176 Died: 1212 
1 CONT Royal titles 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Margaret of Hungary Empress consort of Nicaea
1 CONT 1204–1212 Succeeded by
1 CONT Philippa of Armenia 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT K. Varzos, I genealogia ton Komninon (Thessalonica, 1984). 
1 CONT O city of Byzantium: annals of Niketas Choniates tr. Harry J. Magoulias (Detroit: Wayne State University Press, 1984) especially pages 255–258, 280. 
