0 @N6000000002188002558@ NOTE Leszek I the White
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Leszek I the White (Polish: Leszek Bialy; c.1186 – 1227) was Prince of Sandomierz and (from 1202 or 1206) of Cracow.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Death of Leszek the White, by Jan MatejkoIn 1205 he defeated the Ruthenian army of Prince Roman the Great at the Battle of Zawichost in Lesser Poland.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1227, during a diet of Polish barons at Gasawa, he was assassinated (probably on orders from Duke Swietopelk II of Pomerania).
