0 @N6000000002322305290@ NOTE He was crowned king of Poland on March 4, 1386, the founder of the Jagiellon
1 CONT dynasty, one of 12 sons as heir apparent. He joined two states that became
1 CONT the leading power in eastern Europe, Poland and Lithuania. Though not content
1 CONT to play the role as prince consort, he was, nevertheless, regarded as a
1 CONT foreigner and had to come to terms with a queen who had the prerogartive of
1 CONT acting in her own right. Not until the queen died did he become the leading
1 CONT personality in Poland, ruling thereafter as true King of Poland, to 1434.
