0 @N6000000002187690013@ NOTE Frederick II, Duke of Swabia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Frederick II (1090 – 6 April 1147), called the One-Eyed, "of Hohenstauffen" was duke of Swabia. He was the eldest son of Frederick I, Duke of Swabia, and Agnes of Germany.
1 CONT
1 CONT He succeeded his father in 1105. In 1121 he married Judith of Bavaria, a member of the powerful House of Guelph.
1 CONT
1 CONT On the death of Emperor Henry V, his uncle, Frederick stood for election as King of the Romans with the support of his younger brother Conrad, duke of Franconia and several houses. However, he lost this election of 1125 to Lothar 
1 CONC II, crowned Emperor later in 1133.
1 CONT
1 CONT A conflict erupted between Frederick and his supporters, and Lothar. Encouraged by Albert, Archbishop of Mainz, who loathed the supporters of the late Emperor Henry V, Lothar besieged Nuremberg in 1127. Frederick relieved the sieg
1 CONC e of Nuremberg in 1127 and occupied Speyer in 1128. The attempt of Henry the Proud, duke of Bavaria, to capture Frederick during negotiations failed (1129). However, afterwards supporters of Lothar won a number of victories both i
1 CONC n Germany and in Italy. Speyer (1129), Nuremberg (1130) and Ulm (1134) were captured and in October 1134 Frederick submitted to the emperor. In 1135 both Frederick and Conrad were finally reconciled with Lothar. After Lothar's dea
1 CONC th (1137) and election of Conrad as King of the Romans (1138) Frederick supported his brother in the struggle with Guelphs.
1 CONT
1 CONT Frederick's second wife, Agnes, was the niece of his old enemy Albert of Mainz.
1 CONT
1 CONT According to Otto of Freising, Frederick was "so faithful a knight to his sovereign and so helpful a friend to his uncle that by valor he supported the tottering honor of the realm, fighting manfully against its foes..."
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT Frederick's descendants were:
1 CONT
1 CONT from Judith of Bavaria (d. 1130 or 1131), daughter of Henry IX, Duke of Bavaria 
1 CONT Frederick III Barbarossa (1122-1190), duke of Swabia and Holy Roman Emperor as Frederick I 
1 CONT Berthe of Hohenstaufen (1123-1195), married Matthias I, Duke of Lorraine 
1 CONT from Agnes of Saarbrücken (d.~1147) 
1 CONT Conrad of Hohenstaufen (also called Konrad) (1134/1136-1195), Count Palatine of the Rhine 
1 CONT Judith of Hohenstaufen (1135-1191), married Louis II, Landgrave of Thuringia 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT Otto of Freising 
1 CONT Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis, Lines: 45-25, 166-25 
1 CONT See also: Dukes of Swabia family tree
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] External links
1 CONT Genealogy 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Frederick I Duke of Swabia
1 CONT 1105–1147 Succeeded by
1 CONT Frederick III Barbarossa 
