0 @N6000000002187825777@ NOTE Agnes of Habsburg
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Agnes of Habsburg (ca. 1257 – 11 October 1322) was a daughter of Emperor Rudolph I of Germany and his first wife Countess Gertrude of Hohenberg.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1273 she was married to Elector Albert II of Saxony. They had six children:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Duke Rudolf I of Saxe-Wittenberg (d. 11 March 1356) he was an Elector of Saxony
1 CONT    2. Otto (d. after 29 August 1311)
1 CONT    3. Albrecht (d. 19 May 1342), Bishop of Passau in 1322-1342
1 CONT    4. Wenzel (d. 17 March 1327), a canon in Halberstadt
1 CONT    5. Anna (d. 22 November 1327), married:
1 CONT          1. on 8 August 1308 to Margrave Friedrich der Lahme, son of Frederick I, Margrave of Meissen;
1 CONT          2. on 6 Jule 1315 Duke Henry II of Mecklenburg
1 CONT    6. Elisabeth (d. 1341)
